{"data":[{"slug":"senior-salesforce-administrator-berlin-244565","company_name":"Ninjaone","title":"Senior Salesforce Administrator","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NinjaOne unifies IT to simplify work for nearly 40,000 customers in 140+ countries&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The NinjaOne Unified IT Operations Platform delivers endpoint management, autonomous patching, backup, and remote access in a single console to improve efficiency, increase resilience, and reduce spend. By automating IT and managing all endpoints, organizations give employees a great technology experience at work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;NinjaOne is obsessed with customer success and has retained a 98% customer satisfaction score for more than 5 years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Role Mandate&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A seasoned, hands-on administrator who understands the business problem, scopes and implements complex solutions across Salesforce and connected systems with minimal guidance, and stays accountable for technical quality through delivery and ongoing support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NinjaOne is looking for a Senior Salesforce Administrator to help shape the systems and capabilities that support our growing global revenue organization. As part of Sales Operations, you&#39;ll translate complex business needs into practical, scalable solutions across Salesforce and our connected sales technology ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for someone who combines strong technical judgment with business curiosity and a builder&#39;s mindset. You&#39;ll look beyond the immediate request to understand the underlying problem, challenge unnecessary complexity, and design and build solutions that improve how our teams work. Partnering closely with Salesforce Architects, Admins, our broader Sales Operations teams, and Revenue Stakeholders you&#39;ll guide solutions from discovery and design through implementation and adoption. Your impact will extend beyond individual projects: you&#39;ll help strengthen the architecture, standards, and technical capabilities that allow NinjaOne to scale without continually adding manual work or one-off solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Location - Berlin, Germany&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll be Doing&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate Business Needs into Scalable Solutions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business and Operations stakeholders to understand workflows, identify root causes, and translate priorities into clearly scoped solutions. Challenge assumptions and clarify requirements before moving into a build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop practical recommendations that account for user experience, business impact, dependencies, delivery effort, and long-term maintainability. Explain options and tradeoffs clearly to technical and nontechnical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to Salesforce Solution Architecture&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help scope, design, and implement technical solutions for approved Salesforce initiatives, including data models, automation, access controls, integration requirements, and the impact on existing workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Favor straightforward, maintainable solutions, using native capabilities and low-code tools where appropriate and custom development where justified. Consider scale, performance, security, and support needs before implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect Processes, Data, and Systems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design solutions around end-to-end workflows across Sales, Marketing, Customer Success, and other revenue functions—not isolated requests within a single tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales Integrations, Data &amp;amp; AI, and other technical owners to define system responsibilities, data flows, dependencies, and exception handling. Ensure Salesforce changes work reliably within the broader technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead Technical Delivery and Raise Quality&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain hands-on through prototyping, configuration, complex automation, and troubleshooting. Work alongside administrators and developers through implementation, peer reviews of technical work, and help resolve design challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Salesforce Platform Manager to strengthen testing, version control, deployment practices, and release readiness. Create clear design documentation and support handoffs so solutions can be understood, maintained, and improved by the broader team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build for the Next Stage of Growth&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify technical debt, fragmented workflows, and recurring issues. Recommend phased improvements that address root causes and support new business, customer, and regional requirements without unnecessary customization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Data &amp;amp; AI and Operations teams to evaluate practical automation and AI-enabled improvements. Help define the data, access, integration, testing, and human-review requirements needed to move useful ideas into dependable workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to the Team&#39;s Technical Capabilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical mentorship and constructive design feedback to administrators and developers. Build reusable patterns and shared knowledge that improve delivery quality and reduce reliance on individual experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate risks, dependencies, and recommendations early. Contribute architectural input to the platform roadmap and follow through on the technical outcomes of the initiatives you support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring meaningful Salesforce delivery experience. You have 5+ years of hands-on Salesforce experience, including ownership of solution design and implementation for complex, cross-functional initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong platform fundamentals. You understand Salesforce data architecture, security and sharing, Flow, configuration, and platform constraints. You can assess how design decisions affect reliability, performance, and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can work across configuration and code. You have the technical depth to evaluate Apex and Lightning components, review implementation approaches, and troubleshoot solutions alongside administrators and developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think beyond Salesforce alone. You have experience designing solutions involving connected applications, APIs, and data flows, with a clear understanding of system ownership and downstream impacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand how revenue teams work. You can connect technical decisions to business workflows, user needs, and operational outcomes. You are comfortable turning incomplete or ambiguous requirements into a clear recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take ownership beyond the design document. You bring disciplined testing, documentation, and delivery practices, communicate tradeoffs directly, and stay engaged until a solution works in practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Highly Preferred&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting a high-growth B2B SaaS organization with multiple sales motions, international teams, or evolving customer and partner models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CPQ, routing, sales engagement, and integration platforms such as DealHub, LeanData, Salesloft, or Workato.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving an established Salesforce environment through architectural simplification, automation redesign, integrations, or data migrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant Salesforce certifications, particularly architecture-focused credentials, and experience applying automation or AI to business workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Business priorities become well-defined solutions with clear design decisions and fewer surprises during implementation. Revenue teams experience simpler workflows and less manual work. Salesforce changes fit reliably into connected systems, and the technical team can maintain and extend what has been built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over time, your work should help the organization deliver more consistently, reduce recurring issues and avoidable rework, and support growth without increasing complexity at the same pace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Love &amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Grow personally and professionally with one of the fastest growing companies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enjoy your lunch covered by NinjaOne 3 times/week at the office&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Access to our Corporate Benefits Platform (with discounts for brands such as Expedia, FitX, Zalando and many more)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop your skills through our renowned training platform&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with a curious, kind, international and intercultural workforce  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enjoy your work environment with its location in the heart of Berlin, directly at the Alexanderplatz (close to all transit) &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Additional Information&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is NOT eligible for Visa sponsorship.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(236, 240, 241);&quot;&gt;#LI-MM2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(236, 240, 241);&quot;&gt;#LI-Onsite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, or any other status protected by applicable law. We are committed to providing an inclusive and diverse work environment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Privacy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;When you apply, NinjaOne collects and uses your personal information to review your application and manage the hiring process. To learn how we use, store, and protect your data, and what your rights are, please read our Candidate Privacy Policy at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ninjaone.com/candidate-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;cpp&quot;&gt;https://www.ninjaone.com/candidate-privacy-policy&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/ninjaone/senior-salesforce-administrator-berlin-244565","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":[],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1795578914},{"slug":"engineering-lead-germany-berlin-308123","company_name":"Parallel","title":"Engineering Lead, Germany","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At Parallel, we build AI agents that help healthcare organizations automate their administrative processes and unlock additional revenue, starting with medical coding.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, up to 25% of healthcare spending is lost to manual, repetitive administrative tasks. Legacy software hasn't helped: it has made work slower, more complex and more frustrating for care teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe AI agents can change this. Our technology combines large language models with system-level automation to do real work inside existing hospital tools. No integration, no disruption.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our first agent automates coding and frees up time for medical teams to focus on patients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We launched in 2024 and already have <strong>800+ customers</strong> and a team of 30+ people. We are backed by top-tier investors (Index Ventures, Y Combinator, Hexa, Frst, Kima Ventures, Better Angle and the CEO of Mistral AI), and this is just the beginning.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The future of healthcare isn't just digital, it's automated. Come help us build it!</strong></p><h1>The role</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Context</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Parallel uses AI to take administrative work off hospital teams, starting with inpatient coding. Our agents read the full patient record before billing, find what was documented but not coded, and coders validate every suggestion. We work with around 100 hospitals and clinics in France and are launching in Germany in 2027.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will own our technical roadmap for Germany and be our first engineering leader in the country. You report to Chris Rydhal, CTO and co-founder, and work every day with our General Manager, Germany and our Head of Medical Coding, Germany. Berlin or Munich, hybrid, regular trips to pilot hospitals and to Paris.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Missions</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the German technical roadmap:</strong> decide what we build for Germany and in what order, on top of the core engine we share with Paris.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Adapt our engine to German coding</strong> (ICD-10-GM, OPS, aG-DRG, DKR) with our Head of Medical Coding and AI engineers, and measure its accuracy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run our agents on German hospital information systems</strong> (Dedalus ORBIS first, then CGM, Nexus, Meierhofer, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://i.s.h.med">i.s.h.med</a>, Avelios) through ScreenFlow, our computer-use technology, and handle German data (§21 KHEntgG, §301 SGB V, HL7, FHIR / ISiK).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the technical side of security and compliance:</strong> C5 attestation, hospital security reviews (B3S, NIS2), EU hosting and on-premise deployments when pilots need them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deploy our first German pilots</strong> with our Forward Deployed Engineer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the German engineering team</strong>, as one team with Paris.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In your first months,</strong> you will get ScreenFlow running on Dedalus ORBIS at our first pilot hospital, ship the first version of our German engine with our Head of Medical Coding, drive the technical work for our C5 attestation, and hire our Forward Deployed Engineer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>Who you are</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8 to 12 years in software engineering, including at least 2 years leading a small team or as tech lead. Still hands-on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have shipped software into German hospitals or another regulated health environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have built integrations with hospital information systems (HL7, FHIR, ideally ISiK) and worked with security certifications (C5, ISO 27001, B3S).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">LLMs or ML in production are a plus. <strong>Experience at a KIS, Medizincontrolling or billing software vendor is a big plus.</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A builder and an owner who keeps one product with Paris, not two.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Native German, fluent English.</p></li></ul><h1>Our values</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Play to Win</strong>: we're not here to just take part, deliver something "good enough" or simply enjoy the startup ride. We want to win. That means caring about results, moving fast and bringing the right intensity when it matters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High Trust, High Standards</strong>: trust is our starting point. If you join us, it's because we believe you can own your scope and make good decisions. We don't want a company built on approvals, control and micromanagement. But trust comes with accountability: the more freedom you have, the higher the bar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Low Ego, Hands-On</strong>: at Parallel, no one is above the work. No title, seniority or past success exempts anyone from getting involved in the actual work. Leading means taking responsibility, not distancing yourself from execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Don't Take Yourself Too Seriously</strong>: we take our mission very seriously, not ourselves. Building a company is intense. We want Parallel to remain a place where people enjoy spending time together, laughing, celebrating and giving energy to others. High standards and a good atmosphere aren't opposites: we want both.</p></li></ul><h1>Hiring process</h1><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intro call (30 min).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical deep dive with Chris (60 min): a system you built and the hard calls you made.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design session (90 min, in person or by video): design our first German pilot, end to end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meet the team (General Manager and Head of Medical Coding, Germany), then references.</p></li></ol><h1>Why join us?</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the German product and engineering team from day one, on a founding team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A product already live in around 100 hospitals, an AI engine and computer-use technology built for hospitals that can't wait for long integration projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A competitive package</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We care about who you are, not just what's on your CV.</strong><br />If you're drawn to what we're building but don't meet every requirement, we still want to hear from you. Studies show that women in particular tend to apply only when they meet 100% of the criteria. If that's you, please don't let that hold you back. We'd love to receive your application.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/parallel/engineering-lead-germany-berlin-308123","tags":["Product & Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1795578194},{"slug":"customer-success-manager-smb-german-market-berlin-435003","company_name":"Lexroom","title":"Customer Success Manager | SMB | German Market (Berlin)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.lexroom.ai"><strong>Lexroom</strong></a>, we set the bar for legal AI—clear, fast, and built for trust. In just a few years, what began as an idea has become a reliable platform adopted by <strong>thousands of legal professionals across Europe</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our mission is clear</strong>: <strong>make the law faster, clearer, and more reliable</strong>, giving lawyers, law firms, and companies the time and confidence to focus on what truly matters.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're growing fast, backed by top-tier investors and a world-class team committed to rigor, clarity, and impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, Lexroom is a <strong>trusted partner</strong>, shaping the evolution of legal AI with the same rigor and precision that define our product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us as <strong>Customer Success Manager</strong> to build Lexroom's <strong>German</strong> customer base from the ground up.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be the <strong>first dedicated CS hire for the German market</strong>, owning the full portfolio of <strong>German</strong> customers end to end. The product already won in Italy, with the numbers to prove it. <strong>Germany</strong> is next, and you own it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your key responsibilities</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the full <strong>German</strong> customer portfolio from handover to renewal, with a clear goal: keep every customer (retention first) and grow each account through proactive upsell and uplift.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run a proactive, commercial CS motion. You do not wait for customers to call. You call them, spot the opportunity in every conversation, and bring it home.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the single point of contact for <strong>German</strong> customers, from onboarding and product expertise to support requests, gathering feedback and feeding it back to Product and Marketing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Adapt the Italian playbook to <strong>Germany</strong>, importing what works and localizing it for the <strong>German</strong> market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own your numbers: build dashboards, monitor KPIs, and report on the health and growth of your portfolio.</p></li></ul><h2>What we're looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2 to 4 years in Customer Success or account management, ideally at a SaaS, tech, or software company. Exposure to legal or professional-services customers is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A commercial mindset. You see every customer touch as a chance to add value and expand the account. Direct sales experience is a plus, not a requirement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CRM fluency. Experience working a portfolio in a CRM; HubSpot is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort building in a fast-moving market and staying hands-on, including operational support, while the market scales.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Languages: <strong>native-level German and fluent English are required</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Berlin or willing to relocate.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How we work</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.lexroom.ai"><strong>Lexroom</strong></a> is building the platform where legal work gets done. Founded in Milan in 2023, we are the legal AI built data-first for civil-law Europe: a proprietary base of 7M+ verified legal sources, used today by 12,000+ law firms and in-house legal teams. We recently closed a USD 50M Series B led by Left Lane Capital, with investors including Base10 Partners and Eurazeo, bringing total funding to over USD 73M, to expand across Europe starting with Spain and Germany.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We move fast and accurate, own outcomes, and say what we mean. Impact is defined by execution, not by title.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What Sets Us Apart</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An Exceptional Team.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.lexroom.ai"><strong>Lexroom</strong></a>, you'll work alongside top talent in tech and legal AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our focused teams operate with purpose and autonomy, so every contribution delivers visible results.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll collaborate with people who pair innovation with rigor, curiosity with discipline, ambition with depth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth that Matters.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire exceptional people to make a difference—and we give them space to lead.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your work will shape the future of legal technology and set new standards for the field.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact is defined by vision and execution, not by age or title. If you're ready to take responsibility, you'll find real opportunities to grow and lead high-stakes projects.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Rewarding Your Contribution.</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value excellence and share success:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Annual Salary Range: €65K – 75K€</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity Package: Align your growth with the company's long-term success.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits That Matter</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid Work: Split your time between working from home and collaborating in our <strong>Berlin</strong> office three days a week, with flexibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Performance Bonuses: Rewards tied directly to measurable results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team Retreats &amp; Off-sites: Dedicated time to connect, collaborate, and spark bold ideas.</p></li></ul><h2>Hiring process and timeline</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intro call with our Talent team: motivations, fit, and the essentials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with the Team Manager: your experience and potential for the role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with the <strong>German Team</strong>: get to know each other and discuss upcoming challenges together</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Last step:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meet the Global Head of Customer Success to get to know each other and discuss Lexroom values</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical exercise: a real customer scenario you prepare in advance, then a live call simulation with the Team Manager and the German Team</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At Lexroom, ambition meets discipline and purpose.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're not just building a product—we're setting a new standard for the legal world. If you're ready to contribute to something lasting and meaningful, we'd love to hear from you.</p><hr><p>Compensation: €65K – €75K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • €65K – €75K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/lexroom/customer-success-manager-smb-german-market-berlin-435003","tags":["Customer Success"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1795578194},{"slug":"senior-sales-manager-munich-305658","company_name":"Munich Electrification","title":"Senior Sales Manager (f/m/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Munich Electrification</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Munich Electrification is an innovative company founded with the aim of accelerating the transition to electric and connected mobility. We develop innovative electronic control units for electric vehicles and stationary storage systems for our global customers. Our international team is composed of highly motivated and exceptional engineers. As a small and specialized team we are well-aware of the importance of each individual colleague and support and promote each employee according to their abilities and needs. Our office with adjacent prototype and testing lab is located in the heart of Munich at the Heimeranplatz.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is what we stand for:</p><p styl