isionary mindset, a passion for collaboration, and a commitment to inspire dreams. At ZEAL, we empower our people to think ambitiously and work together toward a shared purpose: helping people imagine and achieve their aspirations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Platform Team (7 DevOps Engineers, 1 Tech Lead, 1 Team Lead) is in the middle of a multi-year modernization journey. As a Senior DevOps Engineer, you will be a hands-on driver of this transformation, not just keeping the lights on, but actively re-architecting how we run our platform at ZEAL</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your Tasks</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, build, and operate reliable, secure, and scalable infrastructure on AWS and On-Prem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help drive the transition of self-managed systems to managed cloud services, minimizing risk and downtime along the way.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement and evolve secrets management and access-control practices in line with security best practices and compliance requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain CI/CD pipelines and developer tooling that let product teams ship safely and frequently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automate provisioning and configuration using Infrastructure-as-Code, reducing manual toil and configuration drift.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain monitoring, logging, and alerting, and manage DNS/CDN/edge security to keep our platforms fast and available.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to multi-region resilience and disaster-recovery capabilities as part of our business continuity efforts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide infrastructure foundations for new business launches, ensuring consistent standards across environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take part in on-call rotation, troubleshoot production incidents, and drive root-cause analysis and postmortems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share knowledge with colleagues, review designs and changes, and help the team continuously raise its engineering standards.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you offer us:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Several years of hands-on experience in a DevOps, Platform, or SRE role, ideally in a production e-commerce or similarly regulated environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong, production-grade experience with AWS and Kubernetes; experience migrating self-managed workloads to managed services (EKS, RDS, MSK, or equivalents) is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience with CI/CD (Jenkins, GitHub Actions) and configuration management / IaC tooling (Ansible, Pulumi, Terraform, or similar).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with databases and streaming systems (PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Kafka) and the operational trade-offs of self-hosting vs. managed services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with secrets management and modern access-management approaches is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with monitoring/observability stacks (Grafana or similar) and edge/CDN platforms (Cloudflare or similar).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of Linux, networking, and security fundamentals; scripting skills (Bash, Python, or Go).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An ownership mindset (“you build it, you own it, you run it”), strong communication skills, and comfort working through ambiguity in a fast-moving modernization effort.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English; German is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What we offer:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li