g>Audit and local filings </strong>- prepare audit requests, support internal and external audits, and handle local statutory and statistical filings for the subsidiaries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product feedback</strong> - use your hands-on knowledge of the Moss platform to give structured feedback to our product teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Rotation</strong> - rotate through other areas of the team and act as backup for colleagues, as we cover every activity twice.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience</strong> in a finance department through an internship, working student role, or similar position.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Educational background</strong> in finance is a plus—such as a degree in finance, accounting, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Solid grasp of bookkeeping fundamentals </strong>(double-entry, reconciliations, period-end close)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience using <strong>automation or AI tools</strong> on real finance work, where in a job, a project or your studies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with working with <strong>data</strong> (SQL, BI tools, or the willingness to learn them quickly)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in both<strong> German (C1) </strong>and<strong> English (C1)</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Genuine interest</strong> and enthusiasm for working in the finance sector.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In addition, here are the <strong>skills and attributes</strong> we are looking for:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Analytical Problem-Solver </strong>– You don’t just identify financial discrepancies—you challenge assumptions, question inefficiencies, and drive solutions. Your critical thinking and problem-solving mindset ensure financial accuracy, compliance, and strategic decision-making in a fast-moving environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Detail-Oriented &amp; Agile</strong> – you care about accuracy and build checks so errors surface early, even when priorities shift.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Process owner </strong>– you own a process end to end, including what happens downstream. You document it, make sure a colleague can cover for you, and automate repetitive work rather than redoing it by hand. You take ownership of tasks, diving deep into the details rather than delegating. Whether it’s resolving posting errors, optimizing liquidity management, or supporting audits, you work independently to find solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compliance-minded</strong> - you work to our policies and audit requirements and know when to escalate tax or transfer pricing questions to the right owner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reliable &amp; Impact-Driven Collaborator </strong>– You go beyond gathering information—you ask the right questions, challenge the status quo, and push for improvements. You excel in cross-functional teamwork, using clear communication and coordination to manage intercompany bookings, oversee accounts payable, and support audits seamlessly.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Moss</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Moss is the Finance AI platform for Europe's mid-sized businesses, giving companies real-time visibility and full control over their spend. By automating card issuing, invoice management and expenses, Moss simplifies financial workflows and frees finance and accounting teams from manual, administrative work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Berlin and used by more than 10,000 businesses including Flink, Schufa, n8n and A