a><em><strong>.</strong></em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/moss/associate-finance-manager-berlin-406339","tags":["Enablement"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1795545613},{"slug":"junior-software-developer-python-web-applications-hamburg-or-berlin-455118","company_name":"Statista","title":"Junior Software Developer - Python & Web Applications (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At <strong>Statista</strong>, we’re all about facts and data, for we are the world's leading business data platform. By providing reliable and easy-to-use data as well as various data analytics products and services, we empower people worldwide to make fact-based decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Hamburg in 2007, we have quickly grown into a global company with offices in major cities such as London, New York, Berlin and Tokyo. And we still have a lot of plans. Our constant growth does not only prove our success, but also keeps creating new development and career opportunities for our employees.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value and celebrate our diverse culture. You are welcome here for who you are, no matter where you come from, what you look like, or whether you prefer bar graphs to pie charts. Your story matters – keep writing it as part of our team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are you ready to join us?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your team</strong><br />This job is with Statista R, a vertical business unit of Statista.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Statista R is a world leader in the creation of company, brand, and product rankings and top lists, based on comprehensive market research and data analysis: Statista R recognizes the best.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With a team of over 100 expert analysts and in cooperation with more than 40 high profile media brands across all continents like Forbes, TIME Magazine and Newsweek, Statista R creates transparency for consumers and business decision makers and helps companies build trust and recognition across a plethora of industries and product categories. A team of over 50 licensing specialists based in New York, Hamburg, Tokyo, and Singapore offers the awarded companies meaningful and eye-catching opportunities to communicate their success via logos and other award related products. Visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://rankings.statista.com"><u>rankings.statista.com</u></a> for further information about Statista R and our rankings.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Role</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, build and maintain web applications for working with data as a core part of your role, mainly using Python frameworks such as Django and Streamlit</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with our senior Data Engineer and other experienced data professionals who build our analytics products and pipelines, learn hands-on about our AWS cloud environment and ETL processes, and help build reliable data pipelines and PostgreSQL queries</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare, transform and validate data so our applications and analyses rest on a solid foundation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create visualizations and insight reports that make findings clear and actionable, both to make our analyst team's processes more efficient and to produce strong client-facing materials</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with teammates to turn analytical questions into usable features and workflows, and develop repeatable ways to build expertise and value for our stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support projects based on large-scale, survey-based market research data, and help develop methods that complement our existing ranking products</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Profile</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid hands-on skills in Python, gained through professional work, internships, research, or your own projects. Experience coding in R is advantageous</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building web applications with Django and/or Streamlit is a strong plus. Knowledge of PostgreSQL or another SQL database, and basic HTML, CSS or JavaScript, is also a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A basic understanding of cloud environments such as AWS and of ETL concepts, and the motivation to grow these skills alongside experienced colleagues</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience working with data, including querying, cleaning, analyzing, visualizing and checking data quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clean coding habits that make teamwork easy, such as readable code and basic Git workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoyment in building tools other people use, a collaborative way of working, and the curiosity to dig into unfamiliar problems</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In addition to our great team, culture, and our shared goal of empowering people with data, there are many other things that make Statista a great place to work! Join us and benefit from:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work from abroad up to 30 calendar days a year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work and flex-time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">International team and social events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Subsidized urban mobility and access to fitness and wellness options</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free access to Langdock and all its amazing functionalities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Career &amp; training opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attractive locations and modern offices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental health support with OpenUp</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Some of the benefits listed here apply only to the German entity and to Junior-level roles or above.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/statista/junior-software-developer-python-web-applications-hamburg-or-berlin-455118","tags":["Tech"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Hamburg or Berlin","created_at":1795545613},{"slug":"junior-analyst-international-ranking-projects-hamburg-or-berlin-459616","company_name":"Statista","title":"Junior Analyst - International Ranking Projects (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">This job is with <strong>Statista R</strong>, a vertical business unit of <strong>Statista</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Statista R</strong> is a world leader in the creation of company, brand, and product rankings and top lists, based on comprehensive market research and data analysis: Statista R recognizes the best.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With a team of over 100 expert analysts and in cooperation with more than 40 high profile media brands across all continents like Forbes, TIME Magazine and Newsweek, Statista R creates transparency for consumers and business decision makers and helps companies build trust and recognition across a plethora of industries and product categories. A team of over 50 licensing specialists based in New York, Hamburg, Tokyo, and Singapore offers the awarded companies meaningful and eye-catching opportunities to communicate their success via logos and other award related products. <br />Visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://rankings.statista.com"><u>rankings.statista.com</u></a> for further information about Statista R and our rankings.<br /><br /><br /><strong>Your Tasks</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support ranking and research projects across industries such as finance, technology and professional services, helping to ensure data quality and transparent results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Research and analyze primary and secondary data for company and market analyses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help set up and run international surveys and analyze their results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use Python, R or SQL to prepare, clean and analyze data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with international clients and media partners, and gradually take on responsibility for project coordination and client communication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn findings into clear presentations and visualizations in Excel and PowerPoint.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Suggest improvements to our rankings, data products and workflows.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Profile</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A bachelor’s or master’s degree in economics, social sciences or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Python, R or SQL, gained through coursework, personal projects, internships or work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound analytical and quantitative skills, paired with an interest in working with data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence using Excel to analyze data and PowerPoint to present findings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in data analysis or research, through projects, study, internships or work is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Effective communication in English; German or other languages are a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A structured, dependable approach to work and an interest in collaborating with colleagues across countries.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In addition to our great team, culture, and our shared goal of empowering people with data, there are many other things that make Statista a great place to work! Join us and benefit from:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work from abroad up to 30 calendar days a year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work and flex-time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">International team and social events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Subsidized urban mobility and access to fitness and wellness options</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free access to Langdock and all its amazing functionalities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Career &amp; training opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Attractive locations and modern offices</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental health support with OpenUp</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Some of the benefits listed here apply only to the German entity and to Junior-level roles or above.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/statista/junior-analyst-international-ranking-projects-hamburg-or-berlin-459616","tags":["Statista R"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Hamburg or Berlin","created_at":1795545613},{"slug":"research-scientist-intern-phd-cohort-27-berlin-203500","company_name":"Prior Labs","title":"Research Scientist Intern (PhD) - Cohort '27","description":"<h2>Who we are</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Foundation models transformed text and images. Structured data - the largest and most consequential data format in the world - stayed untouched, until now. What LLMs did for language, we're doing for tables.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We pioneered tabular foundation models: TabPFN v2 was a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-024-08328-6">Nature</a> cover story, has passed 3.5M+ downloads and 7,500+ GitHub stars, and runs in production from <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.oxcan.org/news/prior-labs-and-oxford-cancer-analytics-partner-to-advance-liquid-biopsy-and-clinical-decision-making-in-lung-disease">detecting lung disease with Oxford Cancer Analytics</a> to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://siliconangle.com/2025/12/01/prior-labs-debuts-tabular-ai-foundation-model-scales-10-million-rows/">preventing train failures with Hitachi</a>. The hardest problems - millions of rows, real-time inference, entirely new modalities - are still open, and no one else is working on them at this level.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://priorlabs.ai/about">small, highly selective team of 40+</a> with backgrounds from Google, DeepMind, Meta, Apple, Amazon, Jane Street, and CERN, led by <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/frank-hutter-9190b24b/">Frank Hutter</a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/noah-hollmann-668b9010b/">Noah Hollmann</a>, and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sauraj-g/">Sauraj Gambhir</a>, and advised by Bernhard Schölkopf and Turing Award winner Yann LeCun.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In July 2026, less than 18 months after our €9M pre-seed, we <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" href="https://priorlabs.ai/blog-posts/priorlabs-sap">joined SAP</a> as an independent frontier AI lab - same team, mission, and open-weights models, now backed by more than €1 billion over four years.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll join our research team for a 4 to 6 month internship, in the cohort that starts in May 2027. The work is hands-on, with tabular foundation models, a new class of AI model, and how they’re applied. We have more open research problems than people to work on them, and you’ll get a project matched to your interests and expertise, with the chance to publish the results. Some of the problems we’re working on:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scaling model architectures and training</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Models that read text and tables together</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architectures for time series, forecasting and anomaly detection</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Faster training and inference</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Causal reasoning in foundation models</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learning across multiple related tables</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benchmarks that show where tabular foundation models work and where they break, in science and in industry</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re doing a PhD in computer science, applied maths, statistics, electrical engineering or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have at least one first-author or shared-first-author paper at a top venue such as NeurIPS, ICML or ICLR.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've turned your own research ideas into working experiments, for example in PyTorch, and you can tell when code is quietly wrong, whether you or a coding agent wrote it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can join us in Freiburg or Berlin from May 2027 for 4 to 6 months.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with data science for tabular data or time series data is a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mentorship at Prior Labs</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your mentor will be one of the researchers building TabPFN, who’ll help you with the technical side of your project and with your development as a researcher. Before you accept, we agree on a project area and a mentor with you, so you know what you’re working on and who you’re working with from day one. During the internship you’ll also work alongside the rest of our research and data science teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A cohort of PhD interns who start with you, and a week-long workshop in Freiburg with the whole cohort in summer 2027</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opportunity to publish your work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compute for your project</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Healthcare, transportation and fitness covered</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key dates</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Applications close on 1 January 2027. We review applications as they arrive, so applying early helps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The cohort starts on 1 May 2027 with a joint onboarding. We can make exceptions, but we’d like you to start with the cohort.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The internship lasts 4 to 6 months, with 6 preferred.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Life at Prior Labs</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work alongside researchers and builders who hold themselves to a very high bar - in the quality of their work and in how they work with each other. We move fast and still take the time to do things right.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our teams are based in Berlin, Freiburg, and New York - when you're working on something as hard as TabPFN, being in the same room matters. But great people come from everywhere, and in exceptional cases we're open to remote, which usually means frequent travel to one of our offices. Wherever you're based, the whole company comes together regularly for offsites to build and celebrate together.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Our Commitments</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The best products and teams are built by people with a wide range of perspectives and backgrounds. We welcome applications from all identities and walks of life - especially if you've ever felt discouraged by "not checking every box" - and provide equal opportunities regardless of gender, sexual orientation, origin, disability, or any other trait that makes you who you are.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We care about how your data is handled - see our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://priorlabs.ai/recruiting-data-privacy">Recruiting Data Privacy</a> page</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/prior-labs/research-scientist-intern-phd-cohort-27-berlin-203500","tags":["Engineering & Science"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1795545613},{"slug":"electrical-engineer-munich-92535","company_name":"pplwise","title":"Electrical Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About pplwise</strong><br />pplwise is a recruiting consultancy for fast-growing technology companies across Europe. Through Recruiting as a Service and Executive Search, we fill key roles for our clients, from start-ups to publicly listed companies. We are filling this position for our client Filics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About our client: Filics</strong><br />Filics is reinventing intralogistics with autonomous mobile robots (AMRs) that change how material moves. Its double-runner system makes Filics the first and only AMR that can drive through load carriers such as Euro pallets. This breaks with forklift logic and sets a new standard for efficiency. Filics is a small, hands-on team that solves hard problems with engineering excellence. Leadership goes to those who take initiative and consistently deliver. As Electrical Engineer (m/f/d) at Filics, you will design the electronics at the core of the next generation of robots.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong><br />This is an on-site/hybrid role in Munich, close to engineering and assembly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Filics doesn’t just use off-the-shelf components. It builds its own custom IP. The robots run on advanced boards that cover a wide range of electrical engineering. On one end is high power, such as battery and motor controllers. On the other end are high-speed interfaces like PCIe, USB and MIPI CSI. The real challenge is making all these subsystems work together as one system. Many of these problems have no textbook solution. Solving them takes solid experience, a deep understanding of the physics and a creative mind.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The EE team is small, and the robot is far from finished. You’ll own your boards <em>end to end</em>: requirements, system design, schematic, layout, design review, sourcing, manufacturing, testing and validation. You’ll keep owning them for as long as they’re in production. You’ll work closely with Embedded Software, Mechanical Engineering, Software and the Production team. As Filics moves from prototypes to series production, your designs need to work reliably at <em>scale</em>, not just in the lab.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take full ownership of a complex PCB project and get it running in as few revisions as possible</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design high-power and high-speed circuits and make sure they work together at system level</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design for EMC, manufacturability and testability, and take boards through EMC testing and certification</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring new technical approaches to the team, for example a new converter architecture that enables higher charging power in a smaller package</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introduce useful processes from your experience, such as simulation workflows that validate a layout before it goes to production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help with board bring-up and debugging together with Embedded Software, and support Production with clear documentation and training</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take over ownership of existing boards so the team shares responsibility</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Several years designing electronics in an R&amp;D environment at a smaller hardware company driven by innovation (e.g. robotics, e-mobility, aviation, autonomous vehicles, motion control)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven record of taking PCBs within a larger system from requirements to a validated product</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong skills in schematic design and PCB layout (Altium, KiCad, OrCAD or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on debugging experience with an oscilloscope, logic analyzer, VNA or spectrum analyzer, plus soldering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with designs that went through EMC testing or CE certification</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An innovator’s mindset: you have <em>built</em> something new or significantly improved an existing concept</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Basic simulation know-how (e.g. LTspice, ANSYS, thermal/EM/tolerance analysis); deeper experience is a strong plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Basic experience with Linux and embedded software</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work independently, take ownership and thrive without rigid structures</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What Filics offers</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real ownership of your designs, from first draft to series production</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Space to innovate and a wide range of technical challenges, from power electronics to high-speed design</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A small, high-caliber team with close collaboration across disciplines</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fast growth: one year at Filics teaches you what usually takes many years at a large company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An on-site/hybrid role in Munich, close to Engineering and Assembly</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sound like you? Apply with your CV.</strong></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/pplwise/electrical-engineer-munich-92535","tags":["🤩 Work with our clients"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Munich","created_at":1795545612},{"slug":"senior-entwicklungsingenieur-mechanik-munich-385211","company_name":"pplwise","title":"Senior Entwicklungsingenieur Mechanik","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Über pplwise</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">pplwise ist eine Recruiting-Beratung für schnell wachsende Technologieunternehmen in ganz Europa. Mit Recruiting as a Service und Executive Search besetzen wir Schlüsselpositionen für unsere Kunden – vom Start-up bis zum börsennotierten Unternehmen. Diese Position besetzen wir für unseren Kunden Filics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Über unseren Kunden: Filics</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Filics erfindet die Intralogistik neu – mit autonomen mobilen Robotern (AMR), die verändern, wie Material bewegt wird. Dank seines Double-Runner-Systems ist Filics der erste und einzige AMR, der durch Ladungsträger wie Europaletten hindurchfahren kann. Das bricht mit der Gabelstapler-Logik und setzt einen neuen Standard für Effizienz. Filics ist ein kleines, praxisorientiertes Team, das schwierige Probleme mit technischer Exzellenz löst. Führung übernimmt, wer Initiative zeigt und zuverlässig liefert. Als <strong>Senior Entwicklungsingenieur -Mechanik</strong> bei Filics leitest du die mechanische Konstruktion der Roboter auf dem Weg vom Prototyp zur Serienfertigung.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Die Rolle</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Die Stelle ist vor Ort/hybrid in München, nah an Entwicklung und Montage.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Filics entwickelt seine Roboter-Hardware komplett selbst: Mechanik, Elektronik und Software. Die Auftragslage wächst, und die Roboter gehen vom Prototyp in die Serie. Konstruktionen, die im Labor funktioniert haben, müssen jetzt zuverlässig, in Stückzahl und zu den richtigen Kosten gebaut werden. Die schwierigsten Probleme liegen oft zwischen den Disziplinen: Teile, die für sich allein funktionieren, können versagen, sobald sie mit der Elektronik verbaut sind.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Das Mechanik-Team besteht aus vier Personen, die meisten am Anfang ihrer Karriere – und sie brauchen jemanden, der sie täglich anleitet. Du bist der technische Lead für die Mechanik des Produkts und das Gegenüber zum Elektronik-Lead, damit sich die aktuelle Mechanik-Leitung auf die Kernentwicklung konzentrieren kann. Deine Zeit teilt sich etwa zur Hälfte auf praktische Ingenieursarbeit und technische Führung auf. Du arbeitest eng mit Elektronik, Produktion, Einkauf und dem CTO zusammen und prägst die Arbeitsweise im Engineering, solange das Team noch klein ist.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deine Aufgaben</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du coachst das Mechanik-Team im Alltag: Du unterstützt bei Konstruktionsentscheidungen, legst Methoden fest und hältst Projekte im Fokus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du konstruierst Bauteile und Baugruppen im CAD inklusive Tolerierung und prüfst jede Konstruktion vor der Freigabe auf Fertigbarkeit und Kosten</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du leitest Test und Integration von Mechanik und Elektronik und löst die Probleme, die erst im zusammengebauten Zustand auftreten</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du priorisierst eingehende Aufgaben, verfolgst den Fortschritt und triffst die täglichen technischen Entscheidungen in der Mechanik</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du setzt den Stage-Gate-Entwicklungsprozess in der Praxis um und führst Design Reviews (Sicherheit, Mechanik, Elektronik, Fertigbarkeit) durch, bevor Teile integriert werden</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du etablierst Design for Manufacturing und Design for Cost: weniger und standardisierte Teile sowie Fertigungsverfahren, die skalieren</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du arbeitest vom ersten Prototyp an eng mit den Elektronik-Verantwortlichen der einzelnen Robotermodule zusammen – und mit der Produktion an Fertigbarkeit und Fertigungsvorrichtungen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du baust Prototypen und entwickelst sie auf Basis von Kunden- und Feldfeedback weiter</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Dein Profil</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mehrjährige praktische Erfahrung in der mechanischen Konstruktion in der Entwicklung eines Unternehmens, das eigene elektromechanische Produkte entwickelt und baut (z. B. Elektrowerkzeuge, Haushaltsgeräte, E-Mobilität, Produktionsmaschinen, Robotik, Schiffsantriebe)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nachweisliche Erfahrung darin, ein elektromechanisches Produkt vom Prototyp in die Serie zu bringen (idealerweise 1.000+ Einheiten pro Jahr) – in einem schnellen Entwicklungszyklus von etwa einem Jahr, nicht in einem jahrzehntelangen Programm</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du konstruierst weiterhin selbst im CAD, vor allem Metallteile und Baugruppen, und bist sicher in der Tolerierung (CAD-Tool egal; Onshape ist ein Plus)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du hast Design for Manufacturing und Design for Cost angewendet und Kosten durch Konstruktion gesenkt: weniger Teile, Normteile</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mindestens zwei Jahre Erfahrung im Mentoring oder in der fachlichen Führung von anderen im Engineering; ein Teamleitungstitel ist nicht erforderlich</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Erfahrung im Testen und in der Integration von Mechanik und Elektronik</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Du hast