&lt;li&gt;Fully Paid Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office stipend based on country of residency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development courses in Cloudbeds University&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to professional development, including manager training, upskilling, and knowledge transfer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;𝗘𝘃𝗲𝗿𝘆𝗼𝗻𝗲 𝗶𝘀 𝗪𝗲𝗹𝗰𝗼𝗺𝗲 - 𝗔 𝗖𝘂𝗹𝘁𝘂𝗿𝗲 𝗼𝗳 𝗜𝗻𝗰𝗹𝘂𝘀𝗶𝗼𝗻&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cloudbeds is proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer that celebrates the diversity in our global team! We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender (including pregnancy, childbirth, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cloudbeds is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. As part of this commitment, Cloudbeds will ensure that persons with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations in the hiring process. We encourage deaf, hard-of-hearing, deaf-blind, and deaf-disabled individuals to apply. If reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process or to perform essential job functions, please contact our HR team by phone at (858) 201-7832 or via email at &lt;a ---------- Cloudbeds will provide an American Sign Language (ASL) interpreter where needed as a reasonable accommodation for the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To all Staffing and Recruiting Agencies: Our Careers Site is only for individuals seeking a job at Cloudbeds. Staffing, recruiting agencies, and individuals being represented by an agency are not authorized to use this site or to submit applications, and any such submissions will be considered unsolicited. Cloudbeds does not accept unsolicited resumes or applications from agencies. Please do not forward resumes to our jobs alias, Cloudbeds employees, or any other company location. Cloudbeds is not responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes/applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-REMOTE&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/cloudbedsthirdpartyboard/staff-software-engineer-revenue-intelligence-285198","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1795578917},{"slug":"it-engineer-london-121214","company_name":"Causaly","title":"IT Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About us:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Causaly is redefining how humans acquire knowledge and develop insights in biomedicine. Our AI-powered platform enables researchers and decision-makers to discover and interpret evidence from millions of scientific publications, clinical trials, regulatory documents, and other complex data sources in minutes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building the world’s most advanced biomedical knowledge platform, powered by a high-precision Knowledge Graph and GenAI capabilities. Our technology is already used by leading biopharmaceutical organizations to accelerate drug discovery, improve safety, and drive better decision-making.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by top-tier investors including ICONIQ, Index Ventures, Pentech, and Marathon, we are scaling rapidly and expanding our product suite and market presence. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an <strong>IT Engineer</strong> to join our IT and Security team and own IT end to end: working with autonomy, automating wherever possible, and helping Causaly's teams find the best IT solution for what they need.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Automate and remove repeat work - </strong>Turn the top request types into automation or self-service, build and maintain workflows</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manage identities and devices – </strong>Manage users and devices life cycle</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manage corporate tools</strong> – Manage corporate tools (SSO, integrations, permission, etc...)</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Prevent, don't just fix - </strong>Spot the patterns behind requests and remove the root cause</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support security </strong>– Work closely with the Security team</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support people</strong> – Support Causaly employees on everything IT related and helping them find the best solution for the problem they want to solve</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Knowledge retention – </strong>Keep IT documentation updated</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years running IT for a cloud-first company of 50-500 people</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong Microsoft and Google Workspace admin capabilities</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scripting and automation</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on with AI tools; able to build and run AI agents that do real work</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive, ownership mindset: you find the problem before users report it</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong documentation and communication skills</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working in GitHub</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with SOC 2 or ISO 27001 evidence</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">SSO/SCIM integrations</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Endpoint management (Intune or similar)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Benefits UK:</u></strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Competitive compensation package  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🩺 Private medical insurance </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🦷 Private dental insurance</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📔 Life insurance (4 x salary)  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤓 Personal development budget </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🧘 Individual wellbeing budget </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌴 25 days holiday plus bank holidays </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🥳 Your birthday off!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 Potential to have real impact and accelerated career growth as a member of an international team that's building a transformative AI product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are on a mission to accelerate scientific breakthroughs for ALL humankind, and we are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applications from all backgrounds and fairly consider qualified candidates without regard to race, ethnic or national origin, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, disability, neurodiversity, genetics, age, religion or belief, marital/civil partnership status, domestic / family status, veteran status or any other difference. </p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/causaly/it-engineer-london-121214","tags":["Technology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795578195},{"slug":"gtm-engineer-london-55076","company_name":"Fleek","title":"GTM Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Can you help us fix the world's most broken supply chain?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The fashion industry produces over 100 billion garments a year. 60% end up in landfill, not because people don't want these clothes, but because the supply chain that moves them from donation to resale is offline, manual and broken.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fleek is fixing this. Our mission is to make secondhand the first choice. We run a B2B marketplace where resellers and stores buy clothing in bulk, and we build the AI systems that digitise the supply chain behind it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our buyers sell on eBay, Vinted, Depop, Whatnot, eBay Live and TikTok Shop, or run vintage stores from Brick Lane to Paris to New York. They source graded stock from wholesalers and rag houses across many countries. Our key enabler is FleekSort, an AI model fine-tuned on secondhand fashion that can grade, price and categorise an item from a single photo.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are now going well beyond vintage. Live sellers can sell almost anything, and there is an opportunity for Fleek to be the backend for B2B resale. We've now started onboarding customers alongside supply from Japan, South Korea, the Philippines and Thailand.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2022, we've saved 9 million items from landfill and tripled in size year on year. We've raised ~$50M from a16z, Y Combinator, HV Capital and others, and recently closed our Series B. Our advisors and private investors include operators behind Depop, Shopify and Postmates.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for people who want to build something that matters, and move fast doing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join the GTM team as our GTM Engineer, reporting to our GTM lead and working day to day with the new business team. You'll own the system we use to find and win customers, on both sides of the marketplace.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">On the demand side, that means online resellers, live sellers and physical stores in the UK, Europe and the US, buying vintage, deadstock, new with tags and luxury. On the supply side, it means the brands, brokers, wholesalers and rag houses who sell to them. As we add new categories and markets, the system has to find those customers too.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We already have pipelines that scrape marketplaces and load leads into our CRM. The next step is everything after that: putting the right leads first, reaching them well, and learning from every outcome. You'll own the engine end to end, from the first scrape to the revenue each new customer brings in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a typical B2B SaaS GTM engineering role. You won't spend your days wiring a CRM to a LinkedIn sequencer or building dashboards. Everyone on our commercial team builds their own tools with AI. You'll take on the problems they can't: systems that improve themselves, infrastructure that scales, and outreach that works within limits set by platforms like Meta.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role is part engineer, part product manager and part commercial. You won't carry a closes target, but you'll own every metric that moves it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The problem you'll solve</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want a system that finds the right customers, puts them in order, reaches out, and gets better every week. It runs as a loop:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find. Source leads across marketplaces and social platforms, for every segment and market we sell into.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prioritise. Score each lead on the signals that predict a good customer, not just a likely reply.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reach out. Contact them on Instagram, WhatsApp, email, phone or LinkedIn, personalised by AI and handed to a rep at the right moment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn. Feed every outcome back into scoring. If a store replied but wasn't a fit, similar leads drop down the list, so we stop spending tokens and rep time on them. Then back to step 1.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">To make that loop work, you'll build a second brain for GTM: one layer that holds everything we know about a customer, with models and agents running on top. That includes the messages we sent and how they replied, how fast they replied and closed, what they sell and where, what they click and search for in our app, what they told our reps on calls, and how much they spend and how well they retain.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The same data powers our account management team, who look after customers once they've placed their first orders. Matching each buyer with the right supply is one of their next big problems, and you'll help solve it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the acquisition engine. Learn how our current pipelines work and improve them. If a rebuild is the right call, make the case for it, and keep leads flowing to the reps while you build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Source at scale in new segments. Find vintage stores, live sellers, deadstock and luxury buyers, and new suppliers, in every market we enter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the scoring and feedback loop. Define what a good lead looks like for each segment, then keep refining it on what actually closes and what actually spends.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engineer multi-channel outreach. Instagram, WhatsApp, email, calls and LinkedIn, personalised by AI and built around real limits like Instagram DM caps and Meta restrictions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the funnel numbers. Leads sourced per day on each platform, reply rate, conversion rate and GMV per close by source. Use them to decide what to fix next.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sit with the reps and talk to customers. Learn why a lead is good and how each segment wants to be sold to. Then automate the repetitive parts of the rep's day.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn repeat work into agents. Qualification, first messages, reply handling, dedupe and CRM hygiene should run without a person.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep it efficient. Every system you build should make sense on cost per lead and unit economics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Connect acquisition to retention. Make sure new customers land cleanly with account management, and help build the buyer-to-supply matching they rely on.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong technical background. You've built and run real systems, such as data pipelines, scrapers, models or production infrastructure. You've done more than configure tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An AI-first mindset, a step ahead. You build with Claude and other models every day and know where agents work and where they break. Our commercial team is very AI-literate, and you'll push them further.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity about the customer. You want to know why one lead closes and another doesn't, and how each segment wants to be sold to. You're happy on a call with a reseller.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Problem solving over playbooks. You take an ambiguous problem, form your own view and ship something that works. We'd rather hire someone who works it out than someone repeating what worked elsewhere.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership. You challenge how things are done, bring your own recommendations and explain why.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rigour with numbers. You track honest metrics, know where your funnel leaks and judge your systems on results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excitement about the space. You see how big the opportunity is and want to build it.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">GTM, growth or RevOps experience, including outbound you've run yourself</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founder or early-startup experience where you owned growth end to end</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building ranking, scoring or recommendation models</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building for marketplaces, resellers, live selling or independent retail</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with secondhand, vintage, deadstock or luxury fashion</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Running multi-channel outbound under platform limits (DM caps, deliverability, warm-up)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What good looks like</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First 30 days: you know the current pipelines inside out, have sat with the reps and have shipped your first improvements, with leads still flowing. You've shared your plan to improve what's there or rebuild it, and why.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3 months: one data layer joins outreach, replies, closes, app activity, call notes and spend. Scoring runs on it, and the loop from outcome back to scoring is live for at least one segment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6 months: the system improves itself. Each week it sources more leads, and better ones, across our segments and markets, and conversion and GMV per close are rising.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">12 months: the engine is the backbone of acquisition across vintage, deadstock and luxury, on both demand and supply. Agents run the repeat work, and you focus on what to build next.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll get</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary plus a performance bonus tied to qualified pipeline</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous equity: being on Fleek means you'll own a part of it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive healthcare coverage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative team in a lovely office in the heart of East London</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to founders. We're a small team and they're heavily involved (and good fun!)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exclusive employee discounts to buy on Fleek</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to borrow any item from our collection of vintage and reworks in the office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A disproportionate level of responsibility and the chance to drive massive impact</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">High ownership, non-hierarchical and fast-moving. We hire problem solvers, not order takers. If you have a better way to do something, and it moves the numbers at a sensible cost, go for it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our commercial team builds its own tools, so each new hire starts more effective than the last. People who deliver get more scope quickly. You'll work embedded with the GTM team, ship fast and see your work in the pipeline within days, not quarters.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The practicalities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Location: London HQ, E1, Spitalfields / Shoreditch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work model: in person, with trust-based flexibility</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stage: post-Series B, hyper-growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team: a GTM team of 5 AEs in new business and 3 AMs in account management, within 100+ people across London, India and Pakistan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Process: an intro call, then an in-person case study in two parts: one on the business with our GTM lead, one technical with our engineers</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our values</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Five values shape how we work at Fleek:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dream Big and Disrupt Yourself: Push the most ambitious version of what you're building. Step out of your comfort zone. Nothing is out of reach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Absolute Ownership: The buck stops with you. Drive initiatives to completion. Experiment, learn, persevere. The job isn't done until the job is done.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity Leads the Way: Don't accept anything at face value. Ask questions you don't know the answer to. That's how you innovate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talk to the Customer: Deeply understand their challenges, motivations and ambitions. Every decision starts with the customer at the centre.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embrace Diversity: A global team building for a global supply chain. Bring your authentic self and embrace the diversity of everyone you encounter.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ready to build the infrastructure for the world's fastest-growing fashion economy? If you want to work on genuinely hard problems, with a world-class team, at a company that's tripling annually, we'd love to hear from you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/job