ing every one of them great, fast, and keeping them there. That’s this role.</p><h2><strong>#2 THE TEAM YOU WILL JOIN</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll report to our VP Sales and work hand in hand with Talent Development, who are building our enablement system: the knowledge hub, the competency framework and the skills data behind it. You make that system real on the ground: on calls, in deals and in 1:1s. You’ll work every day with our Sales Directors, Client Growth Managers, Research Impact Leads and the managers who lead them, and closely with Sales leadership, Product Marketing and GTM Ops.</p><h2><strong>#3 HOW WE OPERATE</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Relentless ownership.</strong> See it. Own it. Don’t wait to be asked.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Low ego, radical candor.</strong> Say the hard thing because you care.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Think AI first.</strong> Start from the agent, not the spreadsheet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Speed.</strong> We execute with the smallest possible team. We work hard and we have fun.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>THE ROLE</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Sales Enablement Lead, you own how our reps and managers get better. You coach in the field, turn our skills and pipeline data into action, and hold reps and managers to the development plans they commit to.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a role for building slide decks or running a learning platform. It’s for someone who has carried a number, knows exactly what good sounds like on a call, and wants to get a whole team performing at that level.</p><h2><strong>YOUR MISSION</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>1. Coach the field</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run weekly call reviews, deal clinics and live sessions across Sales, Client Growth and Research Impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lift the skills that win complex deals: deep discovery, building the business case, multi-threading and closing with a clear next step.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring top performers into the room so what works spreads across the team, and design and run the enablement at our team off-sites.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your bar:</strong> reps feel the difference on their next call, not next quarter.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>2. Coach the coaches</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with every sales manager on how they coach, not just on what their team does.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare managers for 1:1s with each rep’s skills data, and agree development plans together.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your bar:</strong> managers run sharper 1:1s because you’ve been in them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>3. Turn data into action</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Read call-skills scores alongside pipeline, win rates and stage velocity, and spot the patterns by role, region and stage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Decide where coaching goes next, then prove whether it moved the numbers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI agents and practice avatars to scale coaching beyond the hours in your day.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your bar:</strong> every coaching decision has a number behind it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>4. Ramp people and hold the line</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run onboarding for each new cohort of Sales Directors and certify them before they go live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Follow through on every development plan with reps and managers, and report progress to leadership every week.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your bar:</strong> new reps ramp faster, and no development plan goes quiet.</p><h2><strong>WHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In 90 days:</strong> you know every rep, every manager and every deal that matters. A weekly coaching rhythm is live in every region, and every manager has a development plan for each person on their team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In 6 months:</strong> the difference is measurable. Deeper discovery, sharper business cases, and deals that keep moving instead of stalling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In 12 months:</strong> we have a world-class commercial team. New reps ramp in record time, every manager coaches with data, and the best sellers want to join Conveo because of how we develop people.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>WHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must-haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’ve done the job.</strong> A consistent record of hitting quota as an AE or Sales Director in B2B SaaS, selling complex, multi-stakeholder deals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’ve made others better.</strong> As a team lead, player-coach or enablement lead, with results you can point to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You coach managers as well as reps,</strong> and senior sellers take your feedback seriously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You’re fluent with data.</strong> At home in HubSpot (or Salesforce), call-recording tools and dashboards, and you turn numbers into a coaching plan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You hold people accountable,</strong> warmly and directly.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mindset</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.