</p><h2>Our culture</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We put people first and try hard to create an environment where people feel trusted, heard and able to do their best work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value openness, curiosity and different perspectives. You’ll have the freedom to challenge how things are done, experiment with better ways of working and take real ownership of your impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check out our Glassdoor page for the latest reviews or our LinkedIn for company updates and insights from the team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Interview process</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interviewing is a two-way process. Our interviews are conversational, with plenty of time for you to get to know us and ask questions too:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Screening call - 20 mins initial chat with one of our Talent team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First stage – 45 mins competencies-based interview with the hiring manager and IT support analyst</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Second stage – one hour technical interview or assessment with the hiring manager and the Senior TechOps manager</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We review applications as they come in and may close the role once we have enough candidates to move forward. We’ll keep you updated throughout.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Everyone’s welcome</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want to build a diverse and inclusive company full of brilliant people with different skills, experiences and perspectives. All applicants will be considered without regard to age, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, family or parental status, national origin, veteran status, neurodiversity or disability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this sounds like your kind of thing, we encourage you to apply even if you don’t tick every box. <strong>We’d love to hear from you.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><hr><p>Compensation: £27K – £30K</p><ul><li> • £27K – £30K</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/seccl/junior-it-support-analyst-edinburgh-107560","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Edinburgh","created_at":1795578193},{"slug":"ai-solutions-engineer-rd-farringdon-411367","company_name":"Patsnap","title":"AI Solutions Engineer - R&D","description":"<h3>AI Solutions Engineer - R&amp;D</h3><p>&nbsp;</p><p>➡️ <strong>Do you understand how R&amp;D and engineering teams work, from technical research and technology evaluation through to product development and innovation?</strong></p><p>➡️ <strong>Have you gone beyond using AI to actually building solutions, integrating APIs, developing agents or automating complex workflows?</strong></p><p>➡️ <strong>Can you combine hands-on technical capability with the confidence to engage enterprise customers, understand their challenges and design solutions that deliver real value?</strong></p><p class="PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer">&nbsp;</p><p><strong>If this sounds like your next move,&nbsp;we’d love to hear from you.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4><strong>Role Summary:</strong></h4><p class="isSelectedEnd">We have an exciting new role as an AI Solutions Engineer to support our R&amp;D customers.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">You’ll work alongside Account Executives and Account Managers throughout the sales process, speaking directly with prospective customers to understand their R&amp;D and data workflows, uncover what they’re trying to achieve, and design AI-powered solutions around those needs. This isn’t a role where you simply demo an existing product. You’ll be expected to build and tailor the solution for the customer — using Patsnap’s data, APIs, MCP capabilities and AI tools to create agents, workflows, prototypes and proof-of-concepts that bring their use case to life.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="isSelectedEnd">The brief is simple:</p><p><strong>Understand the customer. Build the solution. Prove the value.</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We’re looking for people who can bring together:</p><p><strong>Domain knowledge + customer-facing experience + real AI build capability</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="isSelectedEnd">A typical day could involve joining several customer calls, running technical discovery, building a prototype between meetings, demonstrating it live to a prospect, refining it based on feedback and, where needed, supporting deployment after signature.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>We're looking for someone who brings together three core strengths:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>R&amp;D &amp; Engineering Workflow Understanding:</strong> You understand how R&amp;D, engineering and innovation teams operate, the challenges they face and where AI can deliver value.</p></li><li><p><strong>Customer-Facing &amp; Commercial Capability:</strong> You're confident engaging enterprise customers, leading technical discovery and translating requirements into compelling solutions.</p></li><li><p><strong>Hands-On AI Development:</strong> You can independently build AI agents, integrations, automated workflows and technical prototypes, rather than simply demonstrating existing software.</p></li></ul><p class="isSelectedEnd" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>You'll use Patsnap's proprietary R&amp;D and innovation intelligence, APIs, Model Context Protocol (MCP) capabilities and AI technologies to design, build and demonstrate solutions tailored to customer needs.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>That could involve developing an AI agent to accelerate technical research, integrating Patsnap's intelligence into existing enterprise systems, automating technology scouting processes or creating intelligent workflows to support engineering and product development decisions.</p><p>You'll take customer challenges from initial discovery through to working prototypes and proof-of-concepts, demonstrating how AI can deliver meaningful improvements to their R&amp;D processes.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>This is not a traditional software engineering role. You won’t be expected to build production software from scratch, but you will need to be technically confident, comfortable building independently and credible in front of enterprise customers.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Want to see the platform you'd be representing?</strong><br>Check out this short overview:</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><figure><iframe height="281" width="500" src="//www.youtube.com/embed/j6fCDvnrT2g"></iframe></figure><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><em>This is a hybrid position in our London, UK office, working 1–2 days in the office and the rest from home.</em></p><p>&nbsp;</p><h4><strong>Who are we?</strong></h4><p>Patsnap is a global, pre-IPO company that transforms the way organizations harness their Intellectual Property and Research and Development productivity. Our platform revolutionizes how IP and R&amp;D teams collaborate across the entire innovation lifecycle, using domain-specific AI to accelerate the creation of market-ready products. With over 12,000 customers worldwide, including some of the biggest names in innovation, Patsnap is at the forefront of technological advancement. Our $300M Series E funding round brings our valuation to a $1 billion unicorn status, and we still have a remarkable amount of growth ahead.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>We have a vibrant and diverse team with offices in London, Toronto, Singapore, Shanghai and remote teams based in US. Our hyper-growth trajectory is powered by our people, and we are extremely proud of our company-wide vision, work ethic, and entrepreneurial spirit. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment where talent thrives and ideas bloom.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Why Join Patsnap?</h4><ul><li><p><strong>Build with AI every day.</strong> Design and develop AI agents, technical workflows, integrations and prototypes that address real customer challenges.</p></li><li><p><strong>Work at the forefront of R&amp;D innovation.</strong> Help leading organisations transform how they approach research, technology discovery, engineering and product development.</p></li><li><p><strong>Go beyond traditional pre-sales.</strong> You'll have the freedom to design and build tailored solutions rather than simply demonstrate existing software.</p></li><li><p><strong>Make a tangible commercial impact.</strong> See your technical work directly influence customer decisions, accelerate opportunities and support enterprise adoption.</p></li><li><p><strong>Help shape our AI capabilities.</strong> Work closely with Product and Engineering, bringing real customer requirements into the development of scalable solutions.</p></li><li><p><strong>Join at an exciting stage of growth.</strong> Be part of Patsnap's continued investment in agentic AI, enterprise integrations and the evolution of our Solution Consulting function.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>What You'll Be Doing:</strong></h4><ul><li><p>Partner with Account Executives and Account Managers to support complex enterprise opportunities across R&amp;D, engineering, product development and innovation.</p></li><li><p>Lead technical discovery sessions with customers, understanding their existing research processes, engineering workflows, systems, data requirements and business challenges.</p></li><li><p>Design, build and demonstrate AI agents, intelligent workflows, integrations and proof-of-concepts using Patsnap's APIs, MCP capabilities, LLMs and other relevant technologies.</p></li><li><p>Translate real-world R&amp;D use cases, such as technology scouting, technical literature analysis, engineering research, competitive intelligence and product innovation, into practical AI-powered solutions.</p></li><li><p>Integrate Patsnap's proprietary intelligence into customer workflows, internal systems and AI applications.</p></li><li><p>Deliver tailored technical demonstrations that clearly communicate how proposed solutions address customer challenges and deliver measurable business value.</p></li><li><p>Own proof-of-concept development from initial requirements and solution design through to testing, iteration and customer presentation.</p></li><li><p>Support technical implementation and deployment following signature, collaborating with Product, Engineering and Customer Success where required.</p></li><li><p>Identify opportunities to develop reusable workflows, templates and solution frameworks that can be applied across customers.</p></li><li><p>Share customer insights and technical feedback to help shape Patsnap's future AI capabilities.</p></li><li><p>You won't carry an individual sales quota, but your contribution will be measured through the commercial opportunities you help progress and close.</p></li></ul> <br> <h4><strong>What We'd Love From You:</strong></h4><p class="isSelectedEnd">There are three equally important parts to this role:</p><p><strong>1) R&amp;D &amp; Engineering Workflow Understanding</strong></p><ul><li><p>Strong understanding of R&amp;D and engineering workflows, including how organisations approach technical research, technology scouting, product development, innovation and technical decision-making.</p></li><li><p>Experience working within or supporting engineering, industrial R&amp;D, manufacturing, technology development or other research-intensive environments.</p></li><li><p>Ability to understand the challenges faced by R&amp;D and engineering teams, including fragmented data, complex research processes, information discovery and opportunities for workflow automation.</p></li><li><p>Confidence engaging with technical stakeholders, understanding their requirements and translating these into practical AI-powered solutions.</p></li><li><p>A background in engineering, technical consulting, industrial technology, scientific software or a related discipline would be advantageous.</p></li></ul><p><strong>2) Customer-Facing Experience</strong></p><ul><li><p>Experience working directly with customers or prospects in areas such as pre-sales, solutions consulting, product, implementation, consulting or technical delivery.</p></li><li><p>Confidence leading discovery and requirements conversations.</p></li><li><p>Able to explain complex scientific and technical concepts clearly.</p></li><li><p>Comfortable presenting and demonstrating solutions live.</p></li><li><p>Good commercial judgement: you know when to go deeper technically and when to focus on business value.</p></li></ul><p><strong>3) Hands-On AI Experience</strong></p><p class="isSelectedEnd">You must already have experience building with AI, not simply using LLMs for everyday productivity. </p><p class="isSelectedEnd">We care less about whether something reached production and more about whether you have personally built, tested and iterated something that solved a real problem.</p><p class="isSelectedEnd">That might include:</p><ul><li><p>AI agents or agentic workflows</p></li><li><p>LLM-powered applications</p></li><li><p>APIs and integrations</p></li><li><p>MCP</p></li><li><p>RAG or data-driven AI applications</p></li><li><p>Workflow automation</p></li><li><p>Prompt-based systems</p></li><li><p>Rapid prototypes or proof-of-concepts</p></li></ul><p class="isSelectedEnd">Comfort with APIs, no-code/low-code tools, data and light scripting such as Python is a strong plus.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Backgrounds That Could Fit</strong></p><p class="isSelectedEnd">You mig