">From day one, Insider One’s mission has not only been to build a world-class product company, but also to create one of the</span><b><span style="font-size: 16px"> most socially progressive technology communities</span></b><span style="font-size: 16px"> in the world. Through our social responsibility initiatives like </span><i><span style="font-size: 16px">100 Social Responsibility Projects, AI Training for Teachers, Code Academy, SheCodes, SheLeads, and SheMarkables</span></i><span style="font-size: 16px">, our community has committed to scaling its impact on our communities across 30+ countries, driving initiatives in health, education, farming, animal rights, and increasing women’s representation in STEM.</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style="font-size: 16px">Behind all these achievements is </span><b><span style="font-size: 16px">an exceptionally talented, visionary team of overachievers</span></b><span style="font-size: 16px"> that moves fast and agile, creating cutting-edge products, and focuses on making an impact. If you want to be a part of this journey, just keep reading.</span></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>
<p><strong>About the role</strong></p>
<p>We are looking for a Director, Commercial Partnerships to lead Insider One’s technology and solution partner ecosystem across the United Kingdom, Ireland and the Nordics.</p>
<p>You will own the regional partnership strategy and its commercial results: identifying where partners can accelerate growth, building mutually valuable relationships, and turning those relationships into qualified pipeline, revenue and customer success.</p>
<p>Your portfolio will span complementary technology providers and solution partners, including agencies, consultancies and systems integrators. You will bring these partners together with Insider One’s regional sales and customer teams to develop compelling customer propositions and repeatable routes to market.</p>
<p>This is a hands-on leadership role for someone who combines strategic judgment with strong execution. You should be equally comfortable developing an executive relationship, building a joint business plan and working alongside an account executive to advance an opportunity.</p>
