es</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take day-to-day ownership of the firm’s regulatory framework across the UK and US, prioritising work through a central plan and dashboard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor regulatory developments affecting the business, assess their impact and lead the implementation of any changes required.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with our external compliance provider to keep compliance policies, procedures and controls up to date and applied in practice, including marketing and financial promotions approvals, client categorisation and onboarding, employee compliance (such as personal account dealing, conflicts of interest and gifts and hospitality) and compliance records.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee the compliance monitoring carried out by our external provider, act on its findings, and keep records and evidence ready for regulatory and client due-diligence review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the MLRO and our external provider in running the firm’s financial crime framework, including anti-money laundering, sanctions and client due diligence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assess the regulatory implications of new products, jurisdictions and business initiatives, and coordinate specialist advice where needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a point of contact for regulators and for clients’ and counterparties’ compliance and regulatory teams, including responding to due-diligence questionnaires.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate compliance training with our external provider and promote a strong compliance culture across the business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare regulatory and compliance reporting for the Board and senior leadership, and support corporate governance processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage external legal and regulatory advisers, instructions and budgets, including on contractual, data protection and other matters requiring legal input.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify opportunities to improve compliance processes through templates, automation and technology.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About you</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will have substantial experience in a regulatory or compliance role, whether gained at a fintech, crypto or digital-asset business, a trading firm, bank or broker, a regulator, an advisory or consultancy firm, or a combination of these. A legal qualification is welcome but not required.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in trading, markets, payments or digital assets is desirable. A strong working knowledge of UK regulatory frameworks, sound regulatory judgement and the ability to translate regulatory requirements into practical business processes will be essential. Exposure to US regulation would be an advantage.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You should have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience of compliance frameworks, policies and monitoring, including working with or overseeing outsourced compliance providers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing regulatory change and assessing the regulatory impact of new products or business activities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written communication skills, including drafting clear policies, procedures and reports.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The confidence to work independently and exercise sound judgement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to recognise when specialist legal advice is needed, and to work effectively with external counsel.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A practical, solutions-focused approach, with the ability to explain regulatory requirements clearly to colleagues across the business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to engage confidently with regulators, sophisticated clients, counterparties and their compliance or regulatory teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing external advisers and coordinating work across multiple jurisdictions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An interest in financial markets, trading technology and regulatory developments.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role would suit someone who wants meaningful responsibility in a growing business and enjoys building a well-organised, effective regulatory function rather than simply responding to individual queries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>How to Apply</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please apply directly via this job posting — all applications, including those submitted via LinkedIn, are managed through our applicant tracking system, so you'll always land in the same place regardless of where you found this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Right to Work:</strong> Candidates must have the existing right to work in the UK. We are not currently able to offer visa sponsorship for this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunities:</strong> Reactive Markets is an equal opportunities employer. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates regardless of age, disability, gender reassignment, marriage or civil partnership, pregnancy or maternity, race, religion or belief, sex, or sexual orientation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reasonable Adjustments:</strong> If you need any adjustments or support during the application or interview process, please let us know — we're happy to accommodate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data Protection:</strong> By applying, you consent to Reactive Markets processing your personal data for recruitment purposes, in line with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.reactivemarkets.com/privacy"><u>privacy policy</u></a>.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/reactive-markets/regulatory-lead-united-kingdom-185155","tags":["Finance & Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1795567211},{"slug":"ai-data-engineer-united-kingdom-492838","company_name":"Reactive Markets","title":"AI & Data Engineer","description":"<h1><strong>AI &amp; Data Engineer</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote (UK-based) | Full-Time</strong></p><h2></h2><h2><strong>About Us</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reactive Markets is the <strong>2026 OTC Trading Platform of the Year</strong> (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Risk.net"><u>Risk.net</u></a>). Our network handles over $75 billion in daily trading volumes across FX, Equities, and Cryptocurrency, connecting 60+ of the world's leading liquidity providers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We build trading systems that operate at the edge of what's technically possible — where nanoseconds matter and a dropped message costs real money. Our engineering team is small, senior, and deeply invested in the craft of building cutting edge, reliable, high-performance systems.</p><h2></h2><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a polyglot engineer who is comfortable across the data stack. This is someone who can build AI-powered tools and data infrastructure that make our platform smarter, our people more effective, and our operations more scalable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a research role. You'll build real systems that people use every day — Slack bots that investigate production incidents, data pipelines that surface anomalies before clients notice them, and AI agents that turn hours of manual trawling into seconds of guided investigation. You'll work across the full stack: Python and TypeScript for AI tooling and integrations, Go for backend services, and SQL for data analysis and pipeline work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The person we're looking for ships working software, cares about making people's lives easier, and is energised by the pace of the AI landscape. You don't need to have built LLM applications before — but you should be curious, practical, and comfortable learning fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work closely with our TechOps, Connectivity, and Data teams to understand their workflows, pain points, and knowledge gaps — then build the tools and infrastructure that solve them. This is a high-leverage role: the systems you build will multiply the effectiveness of every engineer and operator in the company.</p><h3></h3><h2><strong>What You'll Work On</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-powered investigation tools</strong> — Slack-based bots and agents that automatically analyse support tickets, query production logs, and surface relevant context for incident response</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers</strong> — authenticated access to ClickHouse, Kubernetes, Atlassian, and GitHub, enabling AI agents to interact with real systems safely</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data infrastructure</strong> — ClickHouse analytics pipelines, real-time anomaly detection, and platform health monitoring (our "Radar" initiative)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI agent development</strong> — constrained, repeatable diagnosis agents that follow investigation playbooks, produce structured outputs, and operate with appropriate guardrails</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Knowledge engineering</strong> — building and curating the corpus that makes our AI tools accurate: documentation, training material, structured metadata, and feedback loops</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Internal tooling</strong> — full-stack applications that bridge the gap between data, AI, and the people who need answers</p></li></ul><h3></h3><h2><strong>What We Need</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong <strong>Python</strong> — your primary language for AI tooling, data pipelines, and backend services</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Systems design – </strong>you have extensive experience building data-intensive systems. You can consider tradeoffs and manage system complexity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>TypeScript / JavaScript</strong> — for Slack integrations, web interfaces, and full-stack tooling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Go</strong> experience is a bonus — we use Go extensively for backend services and CLI tooling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>SQL</strong> — comfortable writing analytical queries against large datasets (ClickHouse, PostgreSQL, or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with <strong>LLM APIs and tooling</strong> — Claude, OpenAI, or similar; prompt engineering, function calling, tool use</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with <strong>Docker, Kubernetes, and AWS</strong> — your tools will run in production infrastructure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Git and Linux fundamentals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in financial services is a plus but not essential — domain knowledge can be learned; engineering instinct cannot</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How you work:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You ship.</strong> You're delivery-focused — you iterate quickly, you get things in front of users, you improve based on feedback</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You bridge domains.</strong> You're comfortable moving between AI, data, infrastructure, and product. You don't wait for someone else to define the interface — you go and understand the problem yourself</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You own it.</strong> When you build something, you take responsibility for its behaviour in production. You monitor it, you fix it, you make it better</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You write things down.</strong> Documentation is how we scale knowledge across a distributed team. Good documentation also makes our AI tools better — every well-written page becomes training material</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You communicate.</strong> We're a distributed team across multiple time zones. Clear, proactive communication is essential</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You embrace AI as a tool.</strong> You use AI to amplify your own productivity — and you build tools that do the same for others</p></li></ul><h3></h3><h2><strong>What You Get</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Growth</strong> — this role sits at the intersection of AI, data, and platform engineering. As the company scales, so does the opportunity. This is a new pod with an exciting remit</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote-friendly</strong> — work from home with flexibility. We trust our people to deliver</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Greenfield AI work</strong> — you're not maintaining legacy systems; you're building the next generation of intelligent tooling for a trading platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real impact</strong> — the tools you build will be used daily by engineers, operators, and eventually clients. This is not a side project</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An excellent team</strong> — senior engineers who care about craft, collaborate openly, and hold each other to high standards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ownership</strong> — small teams, clear accountability, direct impact on the platform and our people</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive package</strong> — up to 30 days leave + bank holidays, private health insurance, pension, life insurance, dental/optical cashback, cycle to work, socials and offsites</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sustainable pace</strong> — we work hard, but we don't burn people out. Balance is how we stay sharp</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in transparency, honest feedback, and writing things down. We celebrate delivery, not activity. We frame AI as empowering people — removing toil, amplifying capability, enabling higher-value work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our Hiring Process</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We keep our process focused and respectful of your time. Our process follows three stages.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stage 1: Initial Conversation</strong> with Talent Acquisition<br /> Format: Video call, ~30-45 minutes</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stage 2: Technical Interview</strong> with a member of the relevant engineering team<br /> Format: Video call, interactive session. ~60 minutes</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stage 3: Leadership Conversation</strong> with our CTO<br /> Format: Video call, ~60 minutes</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What to expect in each stage will be explained by Talent Acquisition if you're invited to interview. Throughout the process, we aim to keep momentum with no unnecessary delays between stages, and feedback typically comes within a few business days.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>How to Apply</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please apply directly via this job posting — all applications, including those submitted via LinkedIn, are managed through our applicant tracking system, so you'll always land in the same place regardless of where you found this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Right to Work:</strong> Candidates must have the existing right to work in the UK. We are not currently able to offer visa sponsorship for this role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunities:</strong> Reactive Markets is an equal opportunities employer. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates regardless of age, disability, gender reassignment, marriage or civil partnership, pregnancy or maternity, race, religion or belief, sex, or sexual orientation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reasonable Adjustments:</strong> If you need any adjustments or support during the application or interview process, please let us know — we're happy to accommodate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Data Protection:</strong> By applying, you consent to Reactive Markets processing your personal data for recruitment purposes, in line with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.reactivemarkets.com/privacy"><u>privacy policy</u></a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">#Hiring #SoftwareEngineering #AI #DataEngineering #FinTech #Python #RemoteWork</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/reactive-markets/ai-data-engineer-united-kingdom-492838","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1795567211},{"slug":"sr-martech-specialist-attribution-performance-london-381609","company_name":"Kraken","title":"Sr. MarTech Specialist, Attribution & Performance","description":"<h1><strong>Building the Future of Open Finance</strong><br /></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payward - the parent company behind Kraken, NinjaTrader, Breakout,  xStocks, Payward Services and CF Benchmarks - has spent the last 15 years building one of the most modern and globally accessible financial infrastructure platforms in the industry, built to advance an open, global financial system.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payward - the parent company behind Kraken, NinjaTrader, Breakout, xStocks, Payward Services and CF Benchmarks - has spent the last 15 years building one of the most modern and globally accessible financial infrastructure platforms in the industry, built to advance an open, global financial system.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2011, Kraken is one of the world's longest-standing crypto platforms, trusted by over 10 million individuals and institutions across the globe. It offers spot trading, margin, futures, staking, and OTC services, with products built for both individual investors and institutional clients.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>The opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Sr. MarTech Specialist for Attribution and Performance, you will support attribution and performance measurement at Payward by owning the data and processes that keep it accurate, and by acting as the bridge between our engineers and our performance marketing team. You will form part of a wider MarTech team and partner closely with finance and compliance so that measurement stays accurate and follows our safety and compliance practices. You will also use AI as a core part of how you work, moving quickly and sharing what you learn with the team. Key responsibilities include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Attribution:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive attribution across web and app, covering conversion definitions, touchpoint credit and journeys stitched together across 3rd party vendors and our inhouse data platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reconcile ad platform, MMP, analytics and internal numbers, and explain the gaps in plain language.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Investigate discrepancies caused by vendor configuration, attribution methodology, fraud or bugs in our own apps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI as part of your everyday workflow to speed up investigation, SQL, specs and reporting, share what works with the team and contribute to team Agent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the roadmap for the next level of attribution, such as incrementality testing, LTV-based optimisation and marketing mix modelling.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineering partnership:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn performance marketing needs into clear specs and tickets for engineering, covering event design, deep links, SDK changes and server-side tracking, and review what ships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with engineers and data owners to keep the signals ad platforms optimise on (Meta, Google and TikTok conversion APIs and postbacks) complete, deduplicated and consent-compliant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Audit and standardise event naming, properties and volume, with monitoring in place to catch breakages early.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Performance and cross-functional support:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run a regular rhythm with performance marketing on attribution health, discrepancies and test readouts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Put a measurement plan in place before spend goes live on new channels, launches and tests, and own the readout afterwards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support weekly and monthly reporting cycles, maintain the attribution dashboards the performance team relies on, and support spend and invoice reconciliation with finance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work directly with MMP and ad platform reps and vendor support, escalating with evidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with compliance to keep tracking, conversion signals and reporting aligned with Payward's safety and compliance practices, including consent, privacy (GDPR, CCPA) and financial promotion rules.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up monitoring and alerts for tracking breakages, fraud and volatility-driven spikes in traffic and conversions, such as sharp market moves, and escalate per policy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Participate in cross-functional discussions with product, compliance, finance, design, data and performance marketing, and prioritise requests openly.</p></li></ul></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What you bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience in MarTech, performance marketing technology, growth analytics or a related digital marketing field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with web and mobile attribution, including MMPs (such as AppsFlyer or Branch), SKAN, deep linking and web-to-app journeys.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of why ad platforms credit conversions differently, and experience with conversion APIs and server-side tracking for Meta, Google Ads and TikTok.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working with data: SQL and a data warehouse, able to read an event schema and trace a discrepancy back to its source.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An AI-native way of working: you already use AI assistants and agents day to day for analysis, SQL, scripting, documentation and automation, move fast with them, check their output before relying on it, and follow our data privacy and security rules when doing so.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working within safety and compliance practices in a regulated environment, such as consent and financial promotion rules, and monitoring data and alerts through volatile periods when traffic and conversions swing quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong stakeholder management and written communication skills, with experience aligning performance marketers, engineers, data, finance and compliance around a number they might not align on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to write a clear spec, work with engineers to deliver it and review the result.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Detail-oriented and process-driven, able to manage multiple workstreams and prioritise the problems that move spend decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine interest in the crypto or fintech industry.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Nice to haves</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to incrementality testing or marketing mix modelling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building AI-assisted workflows or lightweight automations, for example with LLM APIs, scripts or agents, for reporting, QA or monitoring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with affiliate platforms (<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Impact.com">Impact.com</a> or similar), CRM platforms, tag management and consent tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fintech or crypto experience.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Unless a specific application deadline is stated in the job posting, applications are accepted on an ongoing basis.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Please note, applicants are permitted to redact or remove information on their resume that identifies age, date of birth, or dates of attendance at or graduation from an educational institution.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We consider qualified applicants with criminal histories for employment on our team, assessing candidates in a manner consistent with the requirements of the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Our commitment</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payward is powered by people from around the world and we celebrate the diverse talents, backgrounds, contributions, and unique perspectives that everyone brings to the table. We hire based on merit, seeking out people with the right abilities, knowledge, and skills for the job. We encourage you to apply for roles where you don't fully meet the listed requirements, especially if you're passionate or knowledgeable about crypto.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We may ask candidates to complete job-related skills or work-style assessments as part of our hiring process. These assessments evaluate competencies relevant to the role and are applied consistently across candidates for similar positions. Results are considered alongside experience and interviews, and are not the sole basis for any employment decision.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an equal opportunity employer, we don't tolerate discrimination or harassment of any kind, whether based on race, ethnicity, age, gender identity, citizenship, religion, sexual orientation, disability, pregnancy, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic as outlined by federal, state, or local laws.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stay connected</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://twitter.com/krakenfx"><u>Follow us on X</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://blog.kraken.com/#:~:text=Enter%20your%20email%20address"><u>Learn on the Kraken Blog</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="postings-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/kraken-exchange/"><u>Connect on LinkedIn</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.kraken.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice"><u>Candidate Privacy Notice</u></a></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/kraken/sr-martech-specialist-attribution-performance-london-381609","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1795567210},{"slug":"marketing-operations-specialist-seo-aeo-london-250798","company_name":"Kraken","title":"Marketing Operations Specialist, SEO/AEO","description":"<h1><strong>Building the Future of Open Finance</strong><br /></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payward - the parent company behind Kraken, NinjaTrader, Breakout,  xStocks, Payward Services and CF Benchmarks - has spent the last 15 years building one of the most modern and globally accessible financial infrastructure platforms in the industry, built to advance an open, global financial system.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The team</strong></h2><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2011, Kraken is one of the world's longest-standing crypto platforms, trusted by over 10 million individuals and institutions across the globe. It offers spot trading, margin, futures, staking, and OTC services, with products built for both individual investors and institutional clients.<br /><br />The Consumer SEO &amp; AEO team helps people discover Kraken through search engines and AI answers, understand our products and become customers. We connect content, technical SEO, international growth and automation to measurable acquisition, working with Product, Web, Engineering, Data and Compliance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will report to the Head of SEO &amp; AEO and work closely with our SEO &amp; AEO Content Lead. Together, they set priorities and provide strategy, briefs and guidance; you help turn those plans into shipped improvements across the website. Your focus is hands-on SEO/AEO delivery and always-on work, giving both leaders more capacity for GTM, strategy and content direction.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>The opportunity</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the delivery of SEO and AEO improvements across the website, helping turn the team’s strategy into live changes quickly and accurately.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work hands-on in the CMS and other tools to update metadata, internal links, page content, technical SEO and localised pages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check changes in the CMS and on the live site, including links, metadata, formatting and mobile presentation, and follow through on anything that is missing or incorrect.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work cross-functionally with Legal, Compliance, Web, Engineering and Localisation to unblock work, manage feedback and get changes over the line.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use approved AI tools and agents to speed up delivery, while checking outputs, flagging bugs and suggesting improvements to tools and workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compare agreed plans with what is live on the site, spot gaps and opportunities, and keep prioritised work moving when the wider team is busy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and refresh evergreen educational content from SEO and Content briefs, making sure it is useful, search-optimised, accurate and in Kraken’s voice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep Jira and the publishing queue up to date, with clear visibility on what has shipped, what is blocked, what needs a decision and what happens next.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What you bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years of hands-on SEO experience, including implementing website improvements through a CMS, with examples of changes you personally shipped, checked and followed through to completion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand search intent, metadata, internal linking, on-page optimisation and the basics of crawling, indexing, canonical URLs and structured data. You can implement agreed changes and recognise when specialist support is needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can update, build and check pages yourself, and learn unfamiliar publishing and website editing tools with guidance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High attention to detail. You check instructions against the CMS and live website, catch inconsistencies and take responsibility for getting the details right.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You manage agreed priorities, spot gaps, suggest improvements and follow up until work moves forward. You ask questions and seek help early when something is unclear or blocked.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use AI tools to accelerate research, implementation and content work, verify their outputs and give useful feedback when something does not work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An understanding of AEO. You understand how AI search systems find and cite information, why accuracy matters and how to check whether changes improve Kraken’s visibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong writing, editing and fact-checking skills. You can turn a brief or AI-generated draft into useful, search-optimised content that follows brand guidance. You verify product claims and incorporate detailed review feedback accurately.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communication and delivery reporting. You keep tasks current, coordinate with reviewers and technical teams, and explain what has shipped, what is blocked and what needs to happen next. You can use performance data to help assess completed work.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Nice to haves</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Sanity, our content management system, or comparable CMS platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Surfer SEO for content optimisation, Ahrefs for SEO research, Google Search Console for search performance, or equivalent tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Profound or another platform for tracking visibility and citations in AI-generated answers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in crypto, fintech or regulated financial services, including working through Compliance approvals. Familiarity with Adclear, a marketing compliance review tool, is useful.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience implementing localised content and metadata across multiple markets, using AI-assisted workflows alongside language and Compliance reviewers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience improving repeatable workflows through AI agents or automation, including testing outputs, identifying problems and suggesting practical fixes.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><e