and Disney, we push the boundaries of real-time sports data, 3D graphics, and AI-driven storytelling across web and native mobile platforms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're an experienced Senior Product Designer with an exceptional visual craft, deep UX strategy expertise, and a track record of driving complex design initiatives alongside fast-moving engineering squads, this 6-month contract is an exciting opportunity to make a massive impact.<br /><br /></p><h2>What Your Day Will Look Like</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Product Designer, you'll play a pivotal role in shaping how some of the most followed clubs and organizations in world sport engage and inspire millions of fans over the next 9 months on a major project.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working alongside Lead Designers, Product Managers, and cross-functional delivery squads, you'll take full ownership of end-to-end UI and UX execution for major client initiatives across web and native mobile apps (iOS and Android).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">One day you might be architecting complex user journeys and facilitating design workshops for high-stakes fan engagement features. The next, you could be setting component-driven design system standards in Figma, presenting executive-level design rationales to client stakeholders, or mentoring midweight designers within your squad.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll serve as a key creative lead within delivery teams, driving design quality, technical feasibility, and seamless developer handoff. Your work will directly define how millions of sports fans interact with live match data and interactive media worldwide.<br /><br /></p><h2>What We Value</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Beyond Sports, we move fast, collaborate closely, and build things that haven't existed before.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll fit right in if you:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring high-level design craft, producing scalable UI architectures and seamless UX workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take full end-to-end ownership of project workstreams from discovery through design implementation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate complex design strategies clearly to leadership, development teams, and external partners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidently lead client discussions, articulate design decisions, and align multi-disciplinary teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excel at managing your own deliverables, prioritizing high-impact work within active sprint cycles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion continuous design quality and offer constructive feedback to elevate the wider design team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive strong, proactive collaboration across creative, product, engineering, and data teams<br /><br /></p></li></ul><h2>Your Background</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You don't need to tick every box, but we're generally looking for:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Minimum 5+ years of commercial product design experience (agency, high-growth tech, or digital sports media)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A standout portfolio demonstrating complex end-to-end product design, scalable systems, and polished UI/UX for iOS, Android, and responsive web</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced mastery of Figma, including advanced prototyping, tokenized component libraries, and design system governance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep expertise in user-centered design methodologies, information architecture, and responsive design frameworks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience working directly with engineering squads to guide successful design handoff and QA implementation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional project management, time management, and visual/verbal presentation skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable leading design initiatives and collaborating in an English-speaking environment</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Nice to Have (But Not Required)</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep domain knowledge of world sports, live match platforms, sports betting, or real-time data visualization</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing for rich media platforms, 3D/interactive graphics, or streaming interfaces</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with design tokens, CSS/component frameworks, or native mobile HIG and Material Design guidelines<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Why Bring Your Craft to Beyond Sports</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fast-moving, creative, and innovative — that's our world.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Massive Scale &amp; Impact:</strong> Design high-visibility product features used by millions of global sports fans daily</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High Creative Ownership:</strong> Drive key design workstreams autonomously with room to set visual and structural standards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Variety:</strong> Lead design efforts across web platforms, iOS, Android, and emerging immersive sports tech</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborative Squads:</strong> Partner directly with senior product leaders, specialized engineers, and domain experts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Dynamic Environment:</strong> Tackle ambitious 9 to 12-month project milestones within a fast-moving, continuous delivery culture<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Ready to Bring the Beyond Sports Brand to Life?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited about building cutting-edge product experiences, leading impactful design initiatives, and contributing to a brand that's helping redefine sports entertainment, we'd love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Beyond Sports, you won't just design interfaces. You'll help bring sports to life.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/wearebeyondsports/senior-freelance-product-designer-basingstoke-262263","tags":["Beyond Sports"],"job_types":["Contract"],"location":"Basingstoke","created_at":1795567210},{"slug":"project-planner-aberdeen-united-kingdom-195485","company_name":"Xyz Reality","title":"Project Planner - Aberdeen","description":"<h3><strong>About XYZ Reality</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />XYZ Reality created the world’s first engineering-grade augmented reality for construction. Our site-safe hardhat, The Atom, overlays the design model onto the live build, so our engineers can verify work as it goes in on some of the most complex mission-critical projects in the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by Series B investment and growing fast across the US, UK and Europe, we’re a driven, passionate team changing how the industry builds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you want your work to shape how the world gets built, we’d like to hear from you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Help shape the future of construction project delivery with XYZ Reality.</strong></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Customer Operations team is at the heart of project delivery, bringing XYZ Reality's technology to life on site and supporting our clients from initial mobilisation through to successful project handover.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>THE ROLE</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an experienced planning professional to take the lead on programme planning and controls across a portfolio of complex construction projects.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an opportunity to combine your expertise in project planning and scheduling with innovative technology, including 4D planning and augmented reality, to bring greater visibility, accuracy and confidence to project delivery.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our client-facing planning lead, you'll work closely with project teams and stakeholders across multiple locations, identifying risks, challenging assumptions and keeping programmes on track. You'll also collaborate with our Engineering, Production and Sales teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in <strong>Aberdeen, Scotland</strong>, you'll report to the Head of Project Controls Analytics.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>KEY RESPONSIBILITIES</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain project programmes integrated with 3D design models, sequencing the build within the BIM environment in accordance with client requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integrate MEP (Mechanical, Electrical and Plumbing) programmes into the overall project schedule to coordinate multi-disciplinary workstreams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embed the 4D scheduling workflow, linking time-sequenced programme data to the 3D model to enable real-time progress tracking, into project delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead external planning teams, directing their use of Primavera P6, Asta Powerproject, and 4D integration tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify schedule risks and coordination issues across multi-disciplinary workstreams, driving structured resolution with the relevant stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce regular progress reports at both customer and company level, using Microsoft Power BI, Power Apps, and Excel to generate clear, actionable project data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor productivity and completion deadlines, maintaining up-to-date programme status for all active portfolios.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the primary planning contact for clients across active project portfolios, managing relationships proactively throughout the project lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the Sales Team on client calls, demonstrating strong schedule knowledge and the capability of our planning approach</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach and challenge both management and non-specialist audiences on programme matters, operating effectively across technical and non-technical settings</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Minimum 4-6 years of scheduling or programme controls experience in a complex, multi-disciplinary project environment (construction, Oil and Gas, Energy, Infrastructure, Manufacturing, or similar), with demonstrable progression in client-facing or leadership responsibilities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced proficiency in Primavera P6 or equivalent enterprise scheduling platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Senior stakeholder communication and progress reporting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactive, solutions-focused approach to stakeholder management, comfortable challenging assumptions at all levels and sustaining momentum when projects become complex.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Degree in Engineering, Project Management, or a related technical discipline, or equivalent practical experience demonstrating the same level of competence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Right to work in the UK (visa sponsorship is not currently offered).</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>KEY EXPERIENCE &amp; SKILLS</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-directed and comfortable managing ambiguity, able to build planning frameworks rather than simply follow established ones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident operating across technical and non-technical audiences without losing precision or rigour.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative by default, with the confidence to challenge assumptions and hold a position when the programme requires it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine curiosity about technology and how it changes the way projects are planned and delivered.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercially aware, understands the relationship between programme performance and client outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Primavera P6.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Power BI and Power Apps for project data analytics (desirable).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of BIM workflows or 4D model integration (desirable).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to construction or built environment projects (desirable).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience operating in a technology-led or scale-up delivery environment (desirable).</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>BENEFITS</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏝️ 25 days annual leave + public holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎄 Christmas shutdown days on top of your leave allowance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🩺 Private healthcare with Vitality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🪙 Annual salary reviews</p></li><