ftware hasn't helped: it has made work slower, more complex and more frustrating for care teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe AI agents can change this. Our technology combines large language models with system-level automation to do real work inside existing hospital tools. No integration, no disruption.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our first agent automates coding and frees up time for medical teams to focus on patients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We launched in 2024 and already have <strong>800+ customers</strong> and a team of 30+ people. We are backed by top-tier investors (Index Ventures, Y Combinator, Hexa, Frst, Kima Ventures, Better Angle and the CEO of Mistral AI), and this is just the beginning.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The future of healthcare isn't just digital, it's automated. Come help us build it!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The role</strong></h1><h2><strong>Context</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Parallel is growing fast, and so is our invoicing volume. To make sure every signed contract turns into an invoice that is sent and then collected, we are creating the Account Payable Specialist role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own invoicing end to end, from the moment sales sign a contract to collection, working directly with our clients (hospitals and purchasing groups). You report to Bénédicte, Finance Lead, and work day to day with the revenue team and sales, and occasionally with the Deployment Strategists.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Missions</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Taking over at signature</strong>: pick up each contract as soon as sales sign it, check in with the client and connect them with the purchasing group they want to go through.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Client workflow</strong>: drive the process through to the quote and then the invoice, and identify who approves the quote on the client side (not always the person following the invoice).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Invoicing</strong>: send invoices, review quotes and contracts, and invoice every quarter (by bank transfer) in PennyLane.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Follow-up and reminders</strong>: follow up on open files and chase clients, whose response times are long in hospitals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Purchasing groups and direct invoicing</strong>: manage the purchasing groups and direct invoicing through Chorus Pro. When a client goes over the direct invoicing threshold (public entities), contact them to find out which route they prefer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Incoming invoices</strong>: also handle incoming invoices.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In your first months, </strong>you take over every new signed contract as soon as it is signed, and the invoicing route (purchasing group or direct invoicing) is confirmed with the client. You have checked in with the teams of 70 facilities, the first quarterly invoicing run goes out on time and no invoice stays more than 15 days without a reminder. You are the go-to contact for hospitals and purchasing groups on invoicing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Who you are</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You <strong>communicate clearly</strong> and have strong interpersonal skills: you work directly with clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are <strong>autonomous</strong>: you think for yourself, ask the right questions and own a topic end to end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have <strong>at least 2 years of experience in invoicing</strong> (quotes, reminders, collection).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are <strong>comfortable with AI</strong> and already use it in your work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A plus: experience with hospitals or the public sector.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Our values</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Play to Win</strong>: we're not here to just take part, deliver something "good enough" or simply enjoy the startup ride. We want to win. That means caring about results, moving fast and bringing the right intensity when it matters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High Trust, High Standards</strong>: trust is our starting point. If you join us, it's because we believe you can own your scope and make good decisions. We don't want a company built on approvals, control and micromanagement. But trust comes with accountability: the more freedom you have, the higher the bar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Low Ego, Hands-On</strong>: at Parallel, no one is above the work. No title, seniority or past success exempts anyone from getting involved in the actual work. Leading means taking responsibility, not distancing yourself from execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Don't Take Yourself Too Seriously</strong>: we take our mission very seriously, not ourselves. Building a company is intense. We want Parallel to remain a place where people enjoy spending time together, laughing, celebrating and giving energy to others. High standards and a good atmosphere aren't opposites: we want both.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>Hiring process</strong></h1><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conversation with the Hiring Team (30 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conversation with Bénédicte, Finance Lead and your future manager (30 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An afternoon at our office to get a feel for the different aspects of the role and meet the founders (2 hours)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reference check</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h