an 800 hospital clients. We are opening Germany, in Munich, followed by the United States, in New York. We are growing from 40 to 120 people by the end of 2027, across 3 countries. At this pace, the employee experience has to be designed, owned and measured. That's your role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own Parallel's employee experience during its strongest growth phase. Your challenge: make sure every new person is autonomous within 2 weeks, and that our culture holds despite growth and distance. You work hand in hand with Léa, Talent Lead, and you are the People function's point of support on HR and admin topics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Missions</strong></h1><h2><strong>Onboarding</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead onboarding end to end for dozens of new joiners a month, from signature to day 90, in French and English</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define Parallel's onboarding standard and make sure every manager applies it, whatever the site</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run each person's arrival: preparation beforehand, first day, buddy, introduction to the teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the role toolboxes alive with their owners so that every role has up-to-date resources</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the managers' onboarding with Léa (recruiting, 1:1s, performance reviews, HR tools)</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Company life and events</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and run the annual calendar of key moments (seminars, offsites, team buildings, celebrations) for employees across 3 sites</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep team rituals alive, so that the culture is felt as much in Munich and New York as in Paris</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the budget, vendors and logistics of events</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Internal communication</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structure internal communication so that the company's decisions, priorities and news reach everyone at the same time, in every country</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define the channels, formats and information rituals (announcements, newsletter, weeklies)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make arrivals, successes and the company's key moments visible</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Measurement and continuous improvement</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Measure the employee experience: week 2 feedback, satisfaction, time to productivity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analyze feedback and evolve the programs accordingly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benchmark best practices from other growing companies</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Partner to the People function</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take charge of HR admin and operations: personnel register, contracts, internal policies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage office life and benefits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage IT equipment inventory with our vendors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to structuring the People function, including preparing for the 50-employee threshold</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle inbound recruiting, pre-screening calls and the relationship with Welcome to the Jungle</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bridge recruiting and onboarding: you prepare each arrival as soon as the offer is signed</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You will have succeeded if </strong>every new person becomes autonomous faster and their week 2 feedback is positive. Managers apply the same onboarding standard in all 3 countries, our events are looked forward to and well attended, and information flows without teams having to look for it. The People function keeps pace with growth without losin