&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More information about our recruitment philosophy 👉🏻&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/3-tips-pour-briller-en-entretien-star-chez-mirakl-kauffmann-0ojzf/&quot;&gt;https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/3-tips-pour-briller-en-entretien-star-chez-mirakl-kauffmann-0ojzf/&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We welcome collaborators with their diverse perspectives and experiences to power us forward. These often far exceed conventional job requirements and help us create a culture of continuous learning. If you’re ready to join a global leader powering digital transformation for 450+ of the world’s most innovative retailers and B2B organizations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;As part of our recruitment process, Mirakl processes your personal data to review and manage your application and, where appropriate, to consider your profile for future opportunities. You can exercise your data protection rights at any time, and as further detailed in our policies. For more information about how we process your personal data and your rights, please consult our Recruitment Privacy Notice, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mirakl.com/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; in English and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mirakl.com/fr-FR/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; in French.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We may use Artificial Intelligence (AI) solutions to help streamline our hiring process, including screening applications, analyzing resumes, and assessing responses. While AI helps us work efficiently, all final hiring decisions are made by humans. For more information, visit our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://info.mirakl.com/ai-guidelines-for-candidates-and-interviews&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;AI Guidelines for Candidates and Interviews&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mirakllabs/software-engineer-java-freelance-paris-441456","tags":["Tech"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris","created_at":1795568119},{"slug":"product-manager-freelance-paris-67449","company_name":"mirakllabs","title":"Product Manager (Freelance)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mirakl:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2012, Mirakl has been at the forefront of marketplace innovation, empowering every business to compete in the platform economy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Today, Mirakl’s operating system combines an enterprise marketplace solution (Mirakl Platform) that enables retailers and B2B organizations to launch, scale, and operate marketplaces and dropship, AI-powered multichannel selling (Mirakl Connect), retail media (Mirakl Ads) and an agentic commerce infrastructure (Mirakl Nexus).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With dual headquarters in Boston and Paris, Mirakl helps a global ecosystem of 450+ marketplaces (B2C and B2B) and a network of over 100k third-party marketplace sellers. Brands like Macy’s, Decathlon, Carrefour, Asos, and Airbus Helicopters use Mirakl to grow their businesses in new and remarkable ways.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information: &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.mirakl.com&quot;&gt;www.mirakl.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mirakl in Numbers:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🗓️ Founded in 2012 | Member of French Tech Next40&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;👥 750+ employees in 9 offices worldwide: Paris, Barcelona, Bordeaux, Boston, London, Munich, New York, Sydney, Tokyo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🇫🇷 350+ Mirakl Tech teams members mainly based in France&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;⚙️ 5 Saas Solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Mirakl means accelerating your career alongside ambitious, passionate, and supportive colleagues. We&#39;re proud of the diversity of backgrounds, perspectives, and experiences that make our teams unique.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our 5 values guide how we collaborate:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💡&lt;strong&gt; Work Hard Together:&lt;/strong&gt; Teamwork and collaboration are the foundation of our success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🏆 &lt;strong&gt;Get Things Done: &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;We prioritize action and efficiency for impactful results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🚀 &lt;strong&gt;Go Above &amp;amp; Beyond:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; We tackle challenges proactively and always aim for excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🎓 &lt;strong&gt;Succeed Through Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Knowledge sharing and continuous learning are core to our culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🤝 &lt;strong&gt;Satisfy &amp;amp; Empower Clients:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re committed to our clients&#39; success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. The Team You&#39;ll Join&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be part of our Channel Integration team within Mirakl Connect.. We are expanding this team to scale Mirakl Connect&#39;s channel coverage and accelerate the delivery of new in-house marketplace connectors across the platform. Working closely with our Channel Integration PM, Engineering, and other Connect product teams, you&#39;ll drive the growth of Mirakl Connect by launching new strategic sales channels while raising the bar on connector quality and delivery speed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The role requires to be based 4 days a week in our Paris HQ.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Your Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end delivery of new channel connectors: from discovery and scoping with external channels through build, launch, hypercare, and handover to Support, in close collaboration with Engineering and Architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product scoping and execution for your connectors: ground decisions in seller needs, marketplace API requirements, and platform constraints. Write epics and user stories, organize sprints, manage dependencies with other Connect product teams, and track execution end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect launch quality and run beta pilots: define readiness criteria, coordinate functional and technical validation, run beta/pilot phases closely with sellers, and co-own go/no-go decisions with Product and Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own channel documentation and enablement: create and maintain channel documentation for sellers and Support, and collaborate with Product Marketing (PMM) to deliver channel enablement ahead of launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the integration flywheel: turn lessons from each connector into reusable standards, playbooks, and platform improvements, measuring success through time-to-build, delivery predictability, and time to stabilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. What You&#39;ll Bring to the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in product management, program management, or technical project delivery in a SaaS or platform environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of delivering several complex integration projects in parallel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in channel management, e-commerce, marketplaces, or complex software integration models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with APIs, event-driven systems, and software integration lifecycles — you don&#39;t need to code, but you know how to ask the right questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment: ability to lead discovery, challenge requirements, and make pragmatic scope trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder management: influential and constructive, able to build evidence-based points of view and defend them with Product, Engineering, Architecture, external channel contacts, and senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outcome-driven: holds partners accountable while building productive, long-term relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven mindset: comfortable tracking KPIs, measuring delivery quality, and iterating based on insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and adaptable: at ease working cross-functionally in a fast-moving international environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Tech Stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Productboard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Jira&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Languages&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;professional proficiency in French&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;professional proficiency in English&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7. Our Hiring Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We warmly encourage you to apply to any of our roles, even if you think you&#39;re not an exact match.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please click the &quot;Apply&quot; button to submit your application, this helps us make the best possible assessment and get back to you as quickly as possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;45-minute call&lt;/strong&gt; with Mathilde, Talent Acquisition Specialist to discuss your key projects, and present the position in detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1-hour business discussion&lt;/strong&gt; with François Crossette, VP Product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1 x 45-minute STAR interview&lt;/strong&gt; to assess your alignment with our values and meet our Director of Engineering, Jean-Yves Cazac&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More information about our recruitment philosophy 👉&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/3-tips-pour-briller-en-entretien-star-chez-mirakl-kauffmann-0ojzf/&quot;&gt; 3 tips to shine in STAR interviews at Mirakl&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We welcome collaborators with their diverse perspectives and experiences to power us forward. These often far exceed conventional job requirements and help us create a culture of continuous learning. If you’re ready to join a global leader powering digital transformation for 450+ of the world’s most innovative retailers and B2B organizations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;As part of our recruitment process, Mirakl processes your personal data to review and manage your application and, where appropriate, to consider your profile for future opportunities. You can exercise your data protection rights at any time, and as further detailed in our policies. For more information about how we process your personal data and your rights, please consult our Recruitment Privacy Notice, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mirakl.com/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; in English and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mirakl.com/fr-FR/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; in French.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We may use Artificial Intelligence (AI) solutions to help streamline our hiring process, including screening applications, analyzing resumes, and assessing responses. While AI helps us work efficiently, all final hiring decisions are made by humans. For more information, visit our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://info.mirakl.com/ai-guidelines-for-candidates-and-interviews&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;AI Guidelines for Candidates and Interviews&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/mirakllabs/product-manager-freelance-paris-67449","tags":["Tech"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris","created_at":1795568118},{"slug":"head-of-grc-assurance-paris-169731","company_name":"Ledger","title":"Head of GRC & Assurance","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a team of experts pushing the limits of what’s possible, united by our common goal to unlock true freedom through digital ownership, making technology accessible for all. We believe in a world where users, creators and enterprises manage their value with ownership and freedom. Our curiosity drives us to innovate, empowering individuals on a global scale. We believe change is constant and our team moves forward as one, with a culture of problem-solving where every employee is empowered and supported to challenge tradition and create solutions. Our mission is simple: to make self-custody accessible and give people the keys to their own financial futures. If you want to make a true impact, we want you to join us at Ledger.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Ledger, we’re proud to be the global platform for digital assets and Web3, with over 20% of the world’s crypto assets secured through our Ledger devices. With our headquarters in Paris, and offices in Vierzon, Grenoble, Montpellier, London, Portland, Geneva, Zurich and Central Singapore, we have a team of around 600 professionals developing a variety of products and services to enable individuals and companies to securely buy, store, swap, grow and manage crypto assets – including the Ledger hardware wallets line with more than 7.5 millions units already sold in 200 countries.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The team:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join the Security team under the CSO. You will lead Ledger's security risk governance and assurance, emphasise our answers to institutional customers' security requirements, and the evidence that our controls work.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the customer-facing voice of Ledger's risk and assurance position: due diligence, audits, contract security reviews and calls with customer security and risk teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run enterprise security risk governance, the quality of the risk register and the records of risk acceptance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the ISO 27001 programme and prepare SOC 2 readiness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate the legal requirements identified by Legal, including DORA, MiCA and NIS2, into security controls and evidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Govern third-party assurance and assess or coordinate the assessment of controls.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide independent challenge of security controls, and report to the Risk Committee.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and lead the GRC and assurance team, and own its strategy, roadmap and budget, including audit firms and assessors.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">12+ years in security risk, GRC or financial-sector compliance, including 5+ years leading a team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Director-level management experience: you have built a GRC or risk function, owned its budget and audit relationships, and presented to executive committees or boards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expertise in the financial regulation that touches our B2B business, DORA above all, and in risk management (ISO 31000, ISO 27005).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">ISO 27001 lead implementer or lead auditor experience, and a SOC 2 Type II audit you have led.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer-facing experience: bank due diligence, security calls with customer CISOs and risk teams, security answers in tenders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bonus : Experience at a crypto exchange, custodian, payment institution or bank </p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Ledger, we are dedicated to continually investing in our employees which is why we offer more than just salaries; we provide comprehensive compensation packages that include a wide range of benefits. Here are some of the benefits you can look forward to:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible work options - </strong>Our hybrid policy allows employees to work from home up to 3 times per week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness support - </strong>Health and Life Insurance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Financial growth opportunities - </strong>Employees can become shareholders in Ledger as well as other financial benefits depending on your country of work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commuter allowance - </strong>Ledger offers a commuter allowance to contribute to your preferred means of transportation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; Development </strong>- A comprehensive suite of training solutions providing a personalised learning experience for every employee.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">For regionally specific benefits, your Talent Acquisition contact will be able to provide you with more information.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re committed to building an inclusive hiring process. If you need any adjustments or accommodations, just let us know, we’ll do our best to support you.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/ledger/head-of-grc-assurance-paris-169731","tags":["Tech"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1795567212},{"slug":"senior-security-architect-enterprise-saas-paris-219027","company_name":"Ledger","title":"Senior Security Architect - Enterprise & SaaS","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a team of experts pushing the limits of what’s possible, united by our common goal to unlock true freedom through digital ownership, making technology accessible for all. We believe in a world where users, creators and enterprises manage their value with ownership and freedom. Our curiosity drives us to innovate, empowering individuals on a global scale. We believe change is constant and our team moves forward as one, with a culture of problem-solving where every employee is empowered and supported to challenge tradition and create solutions. Our mission is simple: to make self-custody accessible and give people the keys to their own financial futures. If you want to make a true impact, we want you to join us at Ledger.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Ledger, we’re proud to be the global platform for digital assets and Web3, with over 20% of the world’s crypto assets secured through our Ledger devices. With our headquarters in Paris, and offices in Vierzon, Grenoble, Montpellier, London, Portland, Geneva, Zurich and Central Singapore, we have a team of around 600 professionals developing a variety of products and services to enable individuals and companies to securely buy, store, swap, grow and manage crypto assets – including the Ledger hardware wallets line with more than 7.5 millions units already sold in 200 countries.	</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To sustain the company's growth, you'll join the Security Engineering team and will be the hands-on security architect for the applications and SaaS tools Ledger runs on: identity, collaboration, customer support, finance and the vendors behind them. You set the architecture standards, take on the hardest threat models yourself, and make sure data exposure through a vendor or an integration is found by us first.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead threat modelling and risk assessment of enterprise applications, SaaS tools and their integrations, hands-on, starting with the most critical tools and suppliers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the security architecture standards and reusable patterns for enterprise systems: identity and SSO, access and least privilege, endpoints, network access, logging, data protection and integration tokens.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review new applications, SaaS purchases and major changes at design stage, and agree the conditions for going live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design data masking and least-privilege access for customer support and