/jobs/companies/loftorbital/backend-engineer-mission-experiences-toulouse-occitanie-122866","tags":["Mission Platform"],"job_types":["Full time"],"location":"Toulouse, Occitanie","created_at":1795565228},{"slug":"hyrox-operations-associate-stage-paris-431107","company_name":"Lucis","title":"HYROX Operations Associate (stage)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">End-of-studies internship (6 months) · Paris + travel to HYROX races in France · Start ASAP or January 2027</p><h2>About Lucis</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lucis is a preventive health app. A complete blood check-up lets members read a wide range of biomarkers, then get a personalised action plan to improve their health, performance and recovery.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lucis is the National Partner of HYROX France for the 2026-2027 season and title partner of HYROX Toulouse, as part of a three-year partnership. Around it we run an athletes team, a network of partner HYROX gyms, and community events like trainings and shakeout runs.</p><h2>The role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You join the Sport &amp; Athletes team and work directly with Victor, who leads it. You own the operations behind every HYROX race and community events: what has to be ordered, booked, signed, shipped, staffed and paid so that race day just works. On race weekends you are on site, running the booth and the team.</p><h2>What you'll do</h2><h3>HYROX race operations</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the readiness checklist for each race: booth build, suppliers, merch, printing, equipment, lead-capture tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruit, brief and schedule on-site staff and volunteers; build shift plans</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the booth on race days and solve problems live</p></li></ul><h3>Team Lucis athletes</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle athlete admin: contracts, travel and hotel bookings, kit and merch, payments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Send briefs and keep the athlete group informed; track who posted what</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make sure each athlete's check-ups happen on schedule through the season</p></li></ul><h3>Partner gyms and community events</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver activations in partner HYROX gyms: visual assets, event logistics, coach follow-up</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organise community events in collaboration with our events manager (group trainings, shakeout runs) from venue to sign-up page</p></li></ul><h3>Budget, admin and reporting</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the event budget tracker up to date</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">After each race: clean the lead lists, build the recap deck, and follow up with on-site contacts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn what you learn into checklists and templates so each race runs better than the last</p></li></ul><h2>What you bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real event experience: you have already organised or co-run events (sport events, festivals, brand activations, agency work, a student association, a race). Tell us what you owned.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sport is part of your life. You train, compete or coach. HYROX, CrossFit, running, triathlon or team sports: we want to hear about it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organised and reliable. You keep 50 open items moving without dropping one, and people trust your checklists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Calm under pressure. Things break on race day; you fix them and keep smiling at the booth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communicator with suppliers, athletes and partners, in French and English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI-native: you already use AI tools in your daily work (writing, planning, spreadsheets, automation) and check what they produce.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Available for race weekends and some travel across France.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in business school, sport management (STAPS management, sports marketing) or event management.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have raced a HYROX, or worked or volunteered at one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with sponsorship or partner activation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with Notion, Google Sheets, Figma; bonus for no-code tools (n8n, Typeform, Luma)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Driving licence (mandatory)</p></li></ul><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real ownership from day one on one of the fastest-growing sports in France</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A front-row seat at every HYROX France race, with the athletes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A small but highly ambitious and swift team at the crossroads of health, sport and tech</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your own Lucis check-ups</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For interns: a clear path to a CDI if it works out</p></li></ul><h2>How to apply</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Send your CV and a few lines on the best event you ran and the sport you practice. No cover letter needed.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/lucis/hyrox-operations-associate-stage-paris-431107","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1795556416},{"slug":"founding-account-executive-france-paris-45620","company_name":"Condukt","title":"Founding Account Executive (France)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://condukt.co/"><u>Condukt</u></a> is the next-generation compliance platform for financial services, offering an agentic solution powered by real-time data for business identity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Always-on and policy-aware, Condukt enables financial institutions and fintechs to gain actionable insights into business verification - unlocking growth, increasing efficiency, and strengthening compliance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We were founded by former operators and builders with deep experience in banking, payments, and lending. Today, our team spans across London and Porto, bringing together engineers, product owners, and operators from companies like Revolut, Meta, Block (Square), SumUp, American Express, Yandex, and OakNorth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Trusted by leading regulated entities, including Wise, Tide, Mollie, Shift4, Flatpay, and myPOS, Condukt is backed by top investors, including Lightspeed Venture Partners and MMC Ventures.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Position Overview</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Founding Account Executive to lead Condukt's expansion in France, by owning and closing complex, high-value enterprise deals across financial services.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you will lead the full sales cycle, from early discovery and solution design through negotiation and close, working with high-growth fintechs. You'll operate as a trusted advisor to senior decision-makers, helping them navigate complex compliance challenges while unlocking growth with Condukt's real-time identity and AI-powered platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an early-stage, fast-growing company, we value people who take ownership, move with urgency, and are excited to help build both a category-defining product and a repeatable enterprise sales motion. You'll work closely with Account Management, Product, Engineering, and Leadership to shape how we sell, who we sell to, and how we win.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you thrive in consultative enterprise sales, enjoy solving hard problems with customers, and want meaningful influence over strategy and execution, this role is for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Owning France</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is our first hire dedicated to France:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Carry the French number, from pipeline and forecast through to close</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Open the territory from scratch and land our first local reference customers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sell in French, and feed what you hear in the market back to Product</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the full enterprise sales cycle for new strategic customers in France, from first conversation through contract negotiation and close</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead complex, multi-stakeholder deal processes (6+ months), navigating procurement, legal, security, and compliance reviews</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong relationships with senior stakeholders across Risk &amp; Compliance, Product, Operations, and C-suite, positioning Condukt as a long-term strategic partner</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run discovery-led, consultative sales processes that deeply understand customer workflows, regulatory constraints, and success metrics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Craft and deliver executive-level and technical presentations, tailoring value propositions to diverse audiences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely across teams to ensure smooth handoffs, successful implementations, and expansion readiness post-close</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Product and Engineering to shape roadmap priorities, providing structured feedback from the field</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the development of scalable sales playbooks, pricing frameworks, and go-to-market strategy for France</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent Condukt at industry events, conferences, and customer forums, acting as a trusted voice within the fintech ecosystem</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Native or professional French, plus fluent English</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience closing complex enterprise SaaS deals with financial institutions, fintechs, or regulated enterprises</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong track record of exceeding quota in long, consultative sales cycles (6+ months) with multi-six- and seven-figure ACVs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to navigate large, matrixed organizations and influence multiple decision-makers and economic buyers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep commercial acumen paired with strong product intuition, being able to sell value, not just features</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional communication and storytelling skills, equally comfortable with executives and technical stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analytical, structured approach to sales, with comfort working with data, ROI models, and business cases</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-starter mentality with resilience and adaptability in fast-moving, ambiguous environments</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling compliance, risk, identity, fraud, or data infrastructure solutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in fintech, banking, payments, or lending ecosystems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A network in the French fintech or financial-services ecosystem</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prior experience in early-stage or high-growth startups, or as a Founding Account Executive</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with API-first platforms or technical sales motions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working closely with Account Management or Customer Success teams on expansion strategies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional languages (German or Dutch)</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our offer:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tackle meaningful problems with real-world impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary and equity package</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote from France with occasional travels to our London office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flat hierarchy with direct access to the founders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Top-of-the-line equipment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private health insurance, plus sick and compassionate leave as needed</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you have any questions, please reach out to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" ----------<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/condukt/founding-account-executive-france-paris-45620","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1795556415},{"slug":"comptable-fournisseurs-senior-lille-478323","company_name":"Exotec","title":"Comptable Fournisseurs Senior","description":"<p>Chez Exotec, nous mettons l’excellence technologique au service de la redéfinition des relations entre humains et robots. A travers le monde, nos solutions révolutionnent la façon dont nos client·e·s délivrent leurs produits aux personnes consommatrices finales. Nous contribuons au succès des plus grandes marques du commerce et de l’industrie, tout en améliorant les conditions de travail de leurs salarié·e·s.</p><p>Par l’alliance de l’intelligence artificielle et d’un hardware performant, nos robots sont désormais déployés dans le monde entier et leur succès a fait de nous la première licorne industrielle française.</p><p>Rejoindre Exotec, c’est l’opportunité de donner du sens à vos compétences. Grandissez avec nos ExoPeople dans le monde entier pour faire de vos idées, des réalités.</p><p><strong>La révolution robotique portée par Exotec ne fait que commencer, vous en êtes ?</strong></p><p>Nous favorisons un environnement de travail inclusif et équitable, ouvert à tous les genres. Si vous n'avez pas toutes les qualifications requises mais que ce poste vous intéresse, postulez sans hésiter.</p><p>Poste basé à Wasquehal.</p><p></p><p>En tant que Comptable Fournisseurs Senior, vous jouerez un rôle clé dans la fiabilité des comptes fournisseurs et l'optimisation des processus financiers.</p><p><strong>Gestion des factures fournisseurs</strong></p><ul><li>Contrôler et enregistrer les factures fournisseurs dans le respect des normes comptables, fiscales et légales.</li><li>Effectuer le rapprochement des factures avec les bons de commande et les réceptions de marchandises ou services. Vérifier la conformité des taxes, du prix et des termes de paiement.</li><li>Identifier, analyser et résoudre les écarts ou litiges de facturation en collaboration avec les fournisseurs et les équipes internes.</li></ul><p><strong>Gestion de la relation fournisseurs</strong></p><ul><li>Assurer une communication régulière avec les fournisseurs pour le suivi des demandes et la résolution des problématiques.</li><li>Contribuer au maintien de relations de qualité avec les partenaires externes.</li></ul><p><strong>Gestion des paiements</strong></p><ul><li>Participer à la préparation des campagnes de paiement.</li><li>Veiller au respect des échéances de règlement et garantir l'exactitude des paiements effectués.</li></ul><p><strong>Contrôle et clôture comptable</strong></p><ul><li>Garantir la correcte comptabilisation des opérations fournisseurs et leur réconciliation avec le grand livre.</li><li>Analyser et justifier les comptes fournisseurs, notamment les balances âgées.</li><li>Participer activement aux clôtures mensuelles et préparer les écritures d'ajustement nécessaires (charges à payer, provisions, factures non parvenues, etc.).</li></ul><p><strong>Reporting, audit et amélioration continue</strong></p><ul><li>Préparer les documents et analyses requis dans le cadre des audits internes et externes.</li><li>Accompagner et soutenir les comptables fournisseurs sur les processus quotidiens et les bonnes pratiques comptables.</li><li>Participer aux projets d'amélioration continue visant à renforcer l'efficacité des processus, des outils et de l'organisation.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>8 à 10 ans d’expérience en comptabilité fournisseurs, idéalement dans un environnement international et/ou multisites.</li><li>Solide maîtrise des processus Procure-to-Pay (P2P), des principes comptables et des contrôles associés.</li><li>Excellente maîtrise des outils ERP (SAP Public Cloud, Business Central) et&nbsp;Excel.</li><li>Bonnes capacités d’analyse, de résolution de problèmes et de réconciliation comptable.</li><li>Aisance relationnelle et capacité à collaborer efficacement avec les fournisseurs et les parties prenantes internes.</li><li>Sensibilité à l’amélioration continue et à l’automatisation des processus, avec une volonté de contribuer à la transformation de la fonction finance.</li><li>Anglais professionnel requis dans un environnement international</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul><li>Couverture mutuelle et prévoyance santé compétitive</li><li>Politique famille avantageuse</li><li>Programme de mobilité interne et internationale</li><li>Nombreuses opportunités de formation et de développement</li></ul><p></p><p><em>Chez Exotec, nous garantissons l’égalité des chances dans notre processus de recrutement. L’ensemble des candidatures reçues sont étudiées indépendamment de l’âge, du genre, de l’origine, de la religion, de la couleur de peau, de la nationalité, du sexe, du handicap, de l’orientation sexuelle ou de toute autre distinction protégée par la loi.</em></p><p><em>Nous mettons en place un environnement de travail inclusif et respectueux de toutes les différences.<br>En rejoignant le Pacte Parité, Exotec s’engage pour un écosystème French Tech plus paritaire.</em></p><p></p><p></p><p>Pour postuler, veuillez envoyer votre CV. Seul·e·s les candidat·e·s présélectionné·e·s seront contacté·e·s pour les prochaines étapes du processus de recrutement. Au plaisir de recevoir votre candidature ! Si vous postulez à un poste en Europe, veuillez consulter notre politique de confidentialité pour plus de détails.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/exotec/comptable-fournisseurs-senior-lille-478323","tags":["Finance","Logistics and Supply Chain"],"job_types":["Full time"],"location":"Lille, France","created_at":1795551613},{"slug":"software-engineer-drivers-virtualization-paris-255776","company_name":"Arago","title":"Software Engineer — Drivers & Virtualization","description":"<h2><strong>Meet Arago and the Aragonians</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Arago is an AI and computer hardware company whose mission is to drive the course of history forward. We do so by accelerating breakthroughs at the intersection of AI and semiconductors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in 2024 by AI researchers and physicists with deep expertise in photonics, electronics, software, mathematics, and machine learning, Arago brings together a lean team of engineers and scientists from the world’s top companies and research labs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Composed of nine nationalities and operating from hubs in France, North America, and Israel, we believe in great science and fast achievements. Our work is guided by these core principles:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Do great things: </strong>we deliver work we’re proud to sign our name to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High velocity: </strong>speed matters. We move quickly, one step at a time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>One unit: </strong>we’re all in this together, with relationships grounded in trust, respect, and camaraderie.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">Arago is backed by executives from Apple, Arm, Nvidia, Microsoft, and Hugging Face, as well as prominent US and European deeptech venture firms and exited founders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Drivers &amp; Virtualization Engineer, you will own the host-facing software boundary of Arago’s accelerator. Your mission is to ensure our hardware is accessible, secure, and performant across diverse environments—ranging from bare-metal deployments to complex virtualized and multi-device cloud infrastructures. You will focus on building robust kernel-level interfaces where correctness, isolation, and long-term operational safety are paramount.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Required Skills and Experience</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master’s or PhD degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of OS internals, particularly kernel memory management and I/O paths.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of memory safety requirements in kernel space.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven hands-on experience in Linux kernel driver development and kernel modules.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of virtualization fundamentals (KVM, hypervisors).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience with emulation frameworks, specifically QEMU internals or custom device models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with hardware-level protocols: PCIe, DMA, MMIO, and IOMMU.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Language: English at a proficient level. French is a plus.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop and maintain high-performance Linux kernel drivers for Arago’s proprietary accelerator.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Implement communication protocols and virtual device interfaces to bridge hardware and software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage low-level hardware interactions including PCIe, DMA, MMIO, and interrupt handling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enable seamless virtualized access to accelerators using QEMU and KVM.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and implement robust device sharing, passthrough, and isolation mechanisms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure the security of accelerator operations through strict memory protection and resource isolation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Debug complex failures that span the entire stack: from hardware and kernel to hypervisor and guest OS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the scaling of our architecture from single-device setups to large-scale multi-device deployments.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Pay and benefits</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive cash compensation, with final package based on location, experience, and the pay of team members in similar positions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meaningful stock option plan offered at the earliest stage of the company (included in the majority of full time offers).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relocation bonus and coverage of moving expenses for relocation within 20 minutes of the company’s location.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Healthcare coverage (including family-friendly options), pension contributions, professional development support, and 25 days of PTO, in addition to public holidays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership of a key technical domain, with significant vertical and/or horizontal growth opportunities, based on performance and individual drive.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reimbursement of 50% of the public transport subscription fee.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A high-paced, multicultural (with 10 nationalities), and engineering-led environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Our Hiring Process: Your Journey to Arago</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Screening Call : Get to know you beyond your CV.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical meeting : Deep dive into your past projects and technical achievements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CEO Interview : Assess the fit with the team’s culture and long-term vision.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reference Calls: Mandatory calls with your former managers to validate strengths, weaknesses, and work style.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical Assessment: Take-home technical assignment crafted to the role you’re applying for.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final Interview : Discuss your technical assignment and address any remaining questions with team members.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/arago/software-engineer-drivers-virtualization-paris-255776","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris Office","created_at":1795545615},{"slug":"responsable-communication-creation-de-contenus-h-f-cherbourg-en-cotentin-311850","company_name":"Maison Rivage","title":"Responsable Communication & Création de Contenus (H/F)","description":"<p>Création · Community management · Photo · Vidéo</p><p>CDI · Temps plein (43 h) · Annualisation des heures · Du mardi au samedi</p><p>Prise de poste : début / mi-mars 2027</p><p>Rémunération : 2 400 - 2 550 € brut/mois + variable sur objectifs</p><p>Lieu : Cherbourg-en-Cotentin - bureau & établissements</p><p>Maison Rivage, ce sont sept lieux de vie à Cherbourg-en-Cotentin, du centre-ville jusqu'au port : Madame, Mirage, Les Burgers de Colette, Le Vice City, Le Cartel, L'Étrille et Gambino. Et le groupe grandit : plusieurs ouvertures d'établissements sont à venir. Pour raconter tout cela, nous cherchons un profil créatif qui sera nos yeux et notre voix : sur le terrain, appareil photo en main, et sur nos réseaux, au quotidien.</p><p></p><h2>VOS MISSIONS</h2><h2>Réseaux sociaux & communautés</h2><ul><li><p>Animer le compte Instagram du groupe et les comptes Instagram et Facebook des sept établissements</p></li><li><p>Construire le calendrier éditorial de chaque compte avec les responsables de lieux</p></li><li><p>Publier au quotidien : posts, carrousels, stories, reels</p></li><li><p>Répondre aux messages et commentaires, faire vivre les communautés</p></li><li><p>Jeux concours et campagnes sponsorisées (Meta Ads)</p></li></ul><h2>Photo & vidéo</h2><ul><li><p>Shooter et filmer sur le terrain : plats, cocktails, lieux, équipes, ambiances</p></li><li><p>Couvrir en live les soirées et les temps forts de n