ance or AI-based solutions is beneficial.</p></li><li><p>Strong analytical capabilities, a structured approach to problem-solving and the ability to assess complex technical information independently.</p></li><li><p>Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the confidence to challenge established practices constructively and engage with senior decision-makers.</p></li><li><p>High professional integrity, sound judgement and a strong sense of responsibility.</p></li><li><p>Fluent English is required. German and/or French language skills are an additional advantage.</p></li><li><p>Willingness to undertake international business travel, approximately 20 days or more annually.</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Benefits &amp; Culture</strong></p><ul><li><p>Work in an international financial services environment where technology, security and risk management play a central role.</p></li><li><p>Take on a highly visible position with direct exposure to senior stakeholders and strategic decision-making.</p></li><li><p>Enjoy a broad and varied scope of responsibility across technology, cybersecurity and emerging risk areas.</p></li><li><p>Collaborate with experienced professionals from IT, Business, Risk and Governance in a supportive and knowledge-driven environment.</p></li><li><p>Benefit from opportunities for continuous professional development, specialist training and relevant industry certifications.</p></li><li><p>Contribute to meaningful initiatives that strengthen organisational security, resilience and governance.</p></li><li><p>Join a professional culture that values integrity, initiative, collaboration and individual expertise.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/swisspeak-