tdek je de stad op de fiets met Flagship Bike Tours, proef je de sfeer bij Flagship Waffle Experience Amsterdam, en werken we bij Shipyard aan creatieve projecten op en rond het water. Daarnaast hebben we labels zoals Voyage Amsterdam, Captain Jack en Aemstelland, elk met hun eigen stijl en doelgroep. Samen vormen ze één organisatie, maar met verschillende manieren om mensen de stad te laten ervaren.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/flagship-amsterdam/stage-online-marketing-amsterdam-mbo-hbo-wo-191174","tags":["Kantoor"],"job_types":["Entry","internship"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Nederland","created_at":1795566698},{"slug":"senior-decision-scientist-trust-safety-amsterdam-249952","company_name":"Vinteden","title":"Senior Decision Scientist, Trust & Safety","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll become part of the Trust’s Detection team, with a mission to protect the Vinted community from harmful activities and content. The Detection team in the Trust domain is engaged in detecting, understanding, and stopping illegal, dangerous or inappropriate content within the Vinted Marketplace. As a Senior Decision Scientist embedded in a product team, you will become part of a cross-functional team and drive quality decisions by bringing actionable insights from data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead hypothesis-driven product experimentation, translating data into actionable insights and product improvements. You will design and evaluate experiments with support from experienced stakeholders, ensuring rigorous validation of results and a clear, measurable impact, while maintaining high standards of data quality and accessibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, you’ll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with your team and stakeholders to identify strategic opportunities and provide data-driven recommendations and answer critical business questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside other decision scientists to detect and investigate specific fraud patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test and analyse opportunities to validate their value and understand their business impact, using statistical methods and visualisation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select, calculate, and monitor your team&#39;s key performance indicators, proactively flagging issues, running analyses, and understanding root causes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable your team and direct stakeholders to independently leverage data for business insights via self-service dashboards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a data-driven culture by promoting best practices in analytics and decision-making to make data count.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive proven working experience as a Decision Scientist, Data Analyst, Data Scientist or a related position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good analytical thinking and problem-solving skills, with the ability to balance depth of analysis with business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SQL and Python for data analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with BI tools (e.g., Looker, Tableau, Power BI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of statistical methods, such as A/B testing, regression analysis, and other inferential techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly results-oriented and comfortable with iterative processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator who can convincingly present results to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English, both written and spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advantage: experience working in the Trust &amp;amp; Safety or Fraud-related area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advantage: previous experience working in product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work perks&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to benefit from our share options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days of paid annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Newest MacBook models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequent team-building events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office support: we provide IT workstation equipment and a personal budget of up to €540 for home workplace furniture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lunch benefit per working day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A personal monthly budget for shopping on Vinted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collective Defined Contribution Pension plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NS Business Card for your commute to the office by public transport&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company bike leasing scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly budget for a flexible benefits platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from Home allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dog-friendly office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workation policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Better balance holidays with workdays by working remotely! Up to 90 days per year in the EU, of these, 21 days can be spent globally. For non-EU citizens, it&#39;s 21 days worldwide. This can be combined with time off for vacation or personal time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual learning budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each year, you’ll be given a learning budget (starting at €3,000), and a total of up to 10 working days over a 2-year period to support your personal and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our hybrid model, with 2 recommended office days a week, gives you and your team the flexibility to decide if and when you want to work from home, and when to catch up in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from everybody, regardless of your background, identity, or life experiences. Job openings come with guides, not checklists. If you’re excited about a role, but don’t identify with every point in the ‘About you’ section, apply anyway – you might still be the perfect match!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual gross salary range for this position excluding 8% holiday pay is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€67.700&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€91.500 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vinteden/senior-decision-scientist-trust-safety-amsterdam-249952","tags":["Data Science & Analytics"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795546519},{"slug":"product-manager-marketplace-amsterdam-352979","company_name":"Vinteden","title":"Product Manager, Marketplace","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for Product Managers to join Vinted Marketplace. You’ll own a key area, tackling meaningful problems for our business and members. In close partnership with teams across your domain and neighbouring areas, you’ll collaborate with Product Design, Product Analytics, and Engineering - while becoming part of Vinted’s highly driven, fast-moving product leadership group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, you’ll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive and align the vision and product strategy for your ownership area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and set team objectives for the short and long term.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with peers and stakeholders across functions and product teams to identify and prioritise opportunities to improve user experience, success metrics, and enabling capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and oversee the product development cycle, and be accountable for delivering impactful, high-quality products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tackle complex product problems, conduct rigorous product discovery, and scope solutions with clear requirements and trade-off analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Design and Research to identify and prioritise customer needs, market trends, and the competitive landscape; use insights to inform product strategy and feature development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Engineering to manage product roadmaps and delivery planning, continuously executing the strategy and achieving agreed objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Data Science and Analytics to set success criteria; define, track, and interpret product usage metrics; and iterate on A/B testing learnings and the process itself to ensure actionable, data-driven insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate technology considerations, make trade-off decisions, and assess and address technical risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand all aspects of the product development lifecycle and balances product progress with tech debt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at making data-driven decisions, incorporating data, research, and market analysis to drive improvements through actionable strategies and roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply strategic frameworks that treat strategy as a hypothesis, enabling swift adaptation and recalibration when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use agile methodologies to support iterative development, continuous releases, and the integration of customer feedback to improve product quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect user problems with business opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communicator, able to articulate ideas, communicate trade-offs, and establish clear team frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate effectively at different levels of abstraction, translating complex concepts into actionable iterations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about innovation that delivers member value and makes second-hand first choice, while staying adaptable and open to new challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A fast learner and critical thinker with an open mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: Experience delivering across the full product lifecycle, including integrating user feedback, driving prioritisation, running hypothesis-based experiments, executing pre- and post-launch, and iterating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work perks&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to benefit from our share options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days of paid annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Newest MacBook models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Digital mental and emotional health support and Employee Assistant Program (EAP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequent team-building events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office support: we provide IT workstation equipment and a personal budget of up to €540 for home workplace furniture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A daily lunch allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ClassPass (Gym Membership subsidy)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A personal monthly budget for shopping on Vinted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collective Defined Contribution Pension plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An NS mobility card&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to spend up to 90 days per year - 21 of which can be spent working outside of the EU - on workation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dog-friendly office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual Learning Budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in your professional growth! As part of our commitment to continuous learning, we offer an annual learning budget to support your personal and career development through courses, certifications, workshops and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid Work&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve adopted a hybrid workplace model where 2 days in the office are recommended but not enforced. It’s up to you and your team to decide on the exact days you’ll spend working together in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Vinted Group is committed to building an inclusive workplace where people from all walks of life feel a sense of belonging. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, identities and life experiences. At Vinted, all applicants are treated fairly without regard to their race, age, religion or belief, sex, national origin, citizenship, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, or any other protected characteristic.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual gross salary range for this position is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€64.500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€87.300 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vinteden/product-manager-marketplace-amsterdam-352979","tags":["Greenhouse Requisitions"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795546519},{"slug":"engineering-manager-fraud-prevention-amsterdam-238153","company_name":"Vinteden","title":"Engineering Manager, Fraud prevention","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Information about the position&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a technically savvy &lt;strong&gt;Engineering Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to lead the &lt;strong&gt;Sandpipers Team&lt;/strong&gt; within the Marketplace Payments domain. This team owns the tooling for preventing fraudulent payments and fraudulent chargebacks. You will report to the Director of Engineering and work hand in hand with Product and Data peers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, you’ll&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead, coach, and grow a talented team of engineers. Build and maintain a team culture based on trust, commitment, psychological safety, and clear accountability. Conduct ongoing feedback, performance, and compensation reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Discovery &amp;amp; Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with Product Managers and the team during early-stage discovery to map out the technical strategy for future product initiatives and come up with the delivery plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the team’s delivery against the product roadmap while maintaining team&#39;s health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Highly skilled at building engineering teams, hiring new talent, setting clear scope, and managing priorities to keep the team focused and motivated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Foundations:&lt;/strong&gt; Background in backend engineering (ideally handling external API structures, webhook payloads, and cross-service async communication). You are comfortable guiding technical decision-making.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent Communicator &amp;amp; Vendor Coordinator:&lt;/strong&gt; Outstanding stakeholder management skills, with the ability to articulate complex technical ideas clearly and confidently across internal teams (Product, Compliance, Legal) and external global technology providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work perks&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to benefit from our share options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days of paid annual leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Newest MacBook models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for you and your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequent team-building events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office support: we provide IT workstation equipment and a personal budget of up to €540 for home workplace furniture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lunch benefit per working day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A personal monthly budget for shopping on Vinted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collective Defined Contribution Pension plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NS Business Card for your commute to the office by public transport&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company bike leasing scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly budget for a flexible benefits platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A dog-friendly office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workation policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Better balance holidays with workdays by working remotely! Up to 90 days per year in the EU, of these, 21 days can be spent globally. For non-EU citizens, it&#39;s 21 days worldwide. This can be combined with time off for vacation or personal time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual learning budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each year, you’ll be given a learning budget (starting at €3,000), and a total of up to 10 working days over a 2-year period to support your personal and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid work&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our hybrid model, with 2 recommended office days a week, gives you and your team the flexibility to decide if and when you want to work from home, and when to catch up in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from everybody, regardless of your background, identity, or life experiences. Job openings come with guides, not checklists. If you’re excited about a role, but don’t identify with every point in the ‘About you’ section, apply anyway – you might still be the perfect match!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual gross salary range for this position excluding 8% holiday pay is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€97.800&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€132.300 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/vinteden/engineering-manager-fraud-prevention-amsterdam-238153","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795546519},{"slug":"finance-controller-anywhere-in-the-netherlands-364874","company_name":"Dtact","title":"Finance Controller","description":"<h1><strong>Finance Controller</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Netherlands</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Start date: </strong>Q1 2027</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation: </strong>€70k - €80k annually <em>(depending on experience)</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Employment type: </strong>Full-time (contractor if outside Netherlands)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About DTACT</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">DTACT (Data Transform Act) is a data technology company that helps organizations transform complex information into clear, actionable insights. Founded in 2016, we work with government agencies and enterprises across Europe to solve critical data challenges and support better decision-making in areas such as cybersecurity, defense, intelligence, public safety, and critical infrastructure. Built on deep expertise in these domains, we develop innovative solutions that help organizations gain greater visibility, understanding, and control over their data.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a fully remote and internationally distributed company, we combine technical excellence with a collaborative and adaptable way of working. Our mission is simple: to help organizations turn information into action, enabling faster, smarter decisions when they matter most.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Finance Controller to own DTACT’s finance function end-to-end as we continue to scale internationally. Reporting into the COO, you’ll take full ownership of accounting, collections, financial analytics, budgeting, and compliance (including our Dutch statutory obligations) — acting as the single point of accountability for finance in the business today. This is a hands-on, mid-level role: you’ll be expected to run the entire finance function largely on your own in the near term, while also bringing the leadership mindset and ambition to grow the function — and your own role — as DTACT expands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own end-to-end accounting operations — AP/AR, general ledger, and month end/year-end close — ensuring accurate, timely financial reporting.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the full collections process: invoicing, aging follow-up, and cash flow forecasting.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain finance analytics (dashboards, reports) that give leadership clear, real-time visibility into company performance.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the budgeting and forecasting cycle, partnering with department leads to track actuals against plan.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure full compliance with Dutch tax and statutory reporting requirements (VAT, annual accounts) and manage relationships with external accountants, auditors, banks, and tax advisors.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with People Operations on payroll processing and accuracy across jurisdictions, and own administration of the employee Stock Option Plan (ESOP).</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and continuously improve finance processes, technical efficiencies and controls, laying the groundwork as the company grows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5–8 years of progressive finance/accounting experience, including hands-on ownership of a full finance function — ideally within tech in a startup or scale-up environment.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid knowledge of Dutch accounting standards, tax regulations, statutory compliance requirements and payroll.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to independently manage accounting, collections, budgeting, and financial analytics without a large supporting team.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills and financial modeling ability; comfortable turning data into clear, actionable insights.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leadership potential and genuine ambition to grow into a finance leadership role as the team and company scale.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A hands-on, “roll up your sleeves” attitude, paired with the ability to think and plan strategically.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills in English and Dutch.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What's in for you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive compensation and equity participation</strong>, including an Employee Stock Option Plan (ESOP), allowing you to share in DTACT's long-term success.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote-first flexibility</strong>, with the opportunity to work from anywhere within compatible time zones and a schedule that supports both collaboration and personal needs.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A trust-based culture built around asynchronous communication</strong>, empowering people to work independently while staying connected and aligned across teams.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Generous time off</strong>, including vacation days and local public holidays to help you rest, recharge, and maintain a healthy work-life balance.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Home office support</strong>, including high-quality equipment and a budget to create a productive and comfortable workspace.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An international and diverse team</strong>, where English is our company language and collaboration spans multiple countries, backgrounds, and perspectives.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>High-impact work:</strong> DTACT helps organizations in and outside the government with mitigating their vulnerabilities and providing alerts to incoming threats.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>We believe diverse teams build better solutions.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>DTACT welcomes applications from all qualified candidates, regardless of background or identity. We hire based on skills, experience, and potential, and encourage everyone who meets the role requirements to apply.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Please note: </strong>Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. Candidates must be authorized to work in their country of residence.</em> <br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/dtact/finance-controller-anywhere-in-the-netherlands-364874","tags":["Business Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Anywhere in the Netherlands","created_at":1795545615},{"slug":"legal-counsel-netherlands-hybrid-300479","company_name":"Axelera AI","title":"Legal Counsel","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Position Overview</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Axelera AI is a fast-growing AI semiconductor company headquartered in Eindhoven, building high-performance, energy-efficient AI acceleration hardware and software, from the Metis AI platform for edge inference to next-generation AI processing units. We are scaling quickly: new customers, new partners, new markets, and a growing volume of complex commercial deals across the global semiconductor supply chain.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an experienced commercial lawyer to be the engine of our commercial legal function. You will close deals, build the playbooks and processes that let the business move fast without taking on unmanaged risk, and lead how legal operates day to day, with AI in the loop so a lean team delivers more with less. This is a hands-on role with real scope to shape the function as it grows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key responsibilities:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Commercial contracting</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Draft, review and negotiate a high volume of commercial agreements: customer, distribution, reseller and OEM/ODM agreements; sales terms and EULAs; supply and manufacturing agreements (foundry, OSAT, component suppliers); technology and IP licences; software and SaaS agreements; evaluation, early access and development agreements; R&amp;D collaboration and consortium agreements; services and vendor agreements; and MOUs, LOIs and partnership terms.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the trusted, pragmatic adviser to Sales, Product, Engineering, Operations and Finance, giving clear, commercial risk calls at pace.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise on key semiconductor and AI issues: IP ownership and licensing, warranties and liability caps, product liability, export controls and sanctions, data protection and the EU AI Act.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the CFO and Head of Legal on strategic matters, including corporate transactions and board-level work, as needed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Playbooks and scale</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build AI-ready contract playbooks, fallback positions and approval matrices so AI tools and the business can handle routine deals with minimal Legal involvement.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and own a library of standard templates for our core agreement types (e.g. NDA, customer terms, evaluation, distributor, supplier) aligned to our risk appetite.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Train commercial teams on contract basics, negotiation positions and when to escalate to Legal.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Legal operations</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead legal operations: intake and triage, prioritisation, SLAs and reporting on legal workload and turnaround.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the legal tech and AI stack: select, implement and continuously improve AI review and drafting tools, CLM, e-signature and the contract repository, automating repeatable work end to end.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own contract lifecycle management, including obligation tracking, renewals and keeping contract records complete and up to date.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set up clear policies and processes that scale with the company.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Collaboration</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work alongside, supervise and mentor a Junior Legal Counsel, allocating work and reviewing output.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage external counsel efficiently, including scope and budget, and determine which matters are best handled in-house.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report to the Head of Legal (in the interim, the CFO) and help shape the future structure of the legal team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualifications:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Essential</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualified lawyer with 7+ years' PQE in commercial and corporate law, from a leading firm and/or in-house.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Substantial in-house experience in tech, semiconductors, hardware or deep tech, ideally at a scale-up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong track record negotiating complex, high-value international contracts, including IP-heavy and supply chain deals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on use of AI tools in daily legal work, plus experience building playbooks and processes that let a small team scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial judgement that finds the route to yes, and the ability to explain risk simply to senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort with ambiguity, high volume and shifting priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent business English, our working and contract language.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Desirable</em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Semiconductor, AI or embedded systems experience (foundry, licensing, OEM deals).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of export controls (EU dual-use, US EAR), sanctions and the EU AI Act.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience implementing CLM or AI contract tools, prompting, or building no-code automations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience mentoring junior lawyers, or exposure to venture-backed companies and governance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dutch or another European language.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How We Work: AI-First Legal</strong><br />We're building a lean legal function, not scaling by headcount. AI handles first-pass review, redlining, drafting and research, while lawyers focus on judgement and negotiation. Routine work is self-serve through templates and AI-assisted workflows. We measure turnaround and outcomes, and we use AI responsibly, with human review and clear guardrails on confidentiality and accuracy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location</strong><br />Hybrid, with 2 days per week in our Amsterdam or Eindhoven office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is your chance to shape and be part of a dynamic, fast-growing, international organization. We offer an attractive compensation package, including a pension plan, extensive employee insurances and the option to get company shares.   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">An open culture that supports creativity and continual innovation is awaiting you. Collaborative ownership and freedom with responsibility is characteristic for the way we act and work as a team. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At Axelera AI, we wholeheartedly embrace equal opportunity and hold diversity in the highest regard. Our steadfast commitment is to cultivate a warm and inclusive environment that empowers and celebrates every member of our team. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds to join us in shaping the future of AI.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Axelera AI may at times work with external parties (such as recruiters, headhunters, or executive search firms) to support both publicly posted and confidential searches. Our hiring process never involves any payment from candidates, and we will never require you to use a particular paid service to be considered for a role. If you have been approached by someone on our behalf and want to confirm it’s legitimate, please contact us directly at </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="ms-outlook-linkify" ----------<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/axelera-ai/legal-counsel-netherlands-hybrid-300479","tags":["Corporate Functions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands (hybrid)","created_at":1795545613},{"slug":"mainframe-data-engineer-3-to-6-months-contract-amsterdam-446165","company_name":"Belmont Lavan Ltd","title":"Mainframe Data Engineer - 3 to 6 Months Contract","description":"<p>We are seeking an experienced <strong>Senior Data Engineer</strong> with a strong background in designing, deploying, configuring, and managing enterprise-scale data engineering platforms within secure, on-premises and air-gapped environments.</p><p>The ideal candidate will have extensive hands-on experience working with <strong>Apache Hadoop and Apache Spark clusters</strong>, including installation, configuration, administration, troubleshooting, performance optimisation, and workload management in environments with restricted or no internet connectivity.</p><p>This role will support our <strong>Global Data Centre (GDC)</strong> environment, requiring a candidate who understands the operational and technical challenges of delivering robust, scalable, and secure data platforms within isolated infrastructure.</p><p>The successful candidate will work closely with infrastructure, platform, DevOps, and data engineering teams to build and maintain reliable data processing capabilities.</p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul><li>Design, deploy, configure, and maintain Apache Hadoop and Apache Spark clusters in on-premises and air-gapped environments.</li><li>Manage the full lifecycle of Hadoop/Spark platforms, including installation, upgrades, patching, configuration, monitoring, and troubleshooting.</li><li>Develop, implement, and maintain scalable data pipelines for batch and distributed data processing.</li><li>Optimise Spark workloads and Hadoop cluster performance, including resource allocation, job scheduling, and capacity management.</li><li>Work with PostgreSQL and other enterprise data systems to support data integration, storage, and processing requirements.</li><li>Support the deployment and management of containerised applications 