ards.</li></ul><p><strong>3. Containerisation &amp; Platform Engineering</strong></p><ul><li>Experience with Kubernetes-based platform deployments.</li><li>Hands-on experience with Helm charts for application and platform deployments.</li><li>Working knowledge of Istio Service Mesh, including traffic management, service discovery, and secure service-to-service communication.</li><li>Understanding of container orchestration and microservices architecture.</li></ul><p><strong>4. Data Systems &amp; Engineering</strong></p><ul><li>Strong experience with PostgreSQL, including database integration and performance considerations.</li><li>Experience designing, developing, and maintaining data pipelines.</li><li>Understanding of distributed data storage and processing architectures.</li><li>Knowledge of VSAM and integration with legacy enterprise data environments.</li></ul><h2>Preferred / Desirable Skills</h2><ul><li>Experience supporting large-scale enterprise or government data centre environments.</li><li>Familiarity with Linux system administration.</li><li>Experience with infrastructure automation and configuration management.</li><li>Knowledge of data security, access controls, encryption, and secure data handling.</li><li>Experience with monitoring, logging, and platform observability.</li><li>Exposure to DevOps and CI/CD practices in restricted-network environments.</li></ul><h2>Candidate Profile</h2><p>The ideal candidate will be a hands-on technical engineer rather than purely an architectural or theoretical resource. They should be comfortable taking ownership of the deployment, administration, troubleshooting, and ongoing operational management of Hadoop and Spark platforms.</p><p>Candidates must be able to demonstrate practical experience working within environments where internet connectivity is restricted or unavailable, with an understanding of the additional complexities involved in deploying and maintaining enterprise data platforms in such environments.</