&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/flexport/software-engineer-ii-autonomous-supply-chains-amsterdam-120266","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795535739},{"slug":"commercial-account-executive-meta-amsterdam-300572","company_name":"Horizon3Ai","title":"Commercial Account Executive, META","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Get to Know Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Horizon3.ai is a fast-growing, remote cybersecurity company dedicated to the mission of enabling organisations to proactively find and fix and verify exploitable attack vectors before criminals exploit them. Our flagship product,  the NodeZeroTM platform, delivers production-safe autonomous pentests and other key assessment operations that scale across the largest internal, external, cloud, and hybrid cloud environments. NodeZero has been adopted by organisations of all sizes, from small educational institutions to government agencies and Global 100 enterprises. It is used by ITOps/SecOps teams, consulting pentesters, and MSSPs and MSPs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a fusion of former U.S. Special Operations cyber operators, startup engineers, and formerly frustrated cybersecurity practitioners. We're committed to helping solve our common security problems: ineffective security tools, false positives resulting in alert fatigue, blind spots, "checkbox” security culture, cybersecurity skills shortage, and the long lead time and expense of hiring outside consultants. Collectively, we are a team of learn it alls, committed to a culture of respect, collaboration, ownership, and results.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Description</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help shape the next stage of Horizon3.ai’s META growth. Based in the Netherlands with regular travel to the region, you’ll bring autonomous pentesting to new customers and help them reduce real-world security risk. If you thrive on opening doors, building partnerships and turning opportunities into wins, this is a chance to make a visible impact as we expand our META Commercial team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We currently require our Amsterdam team to come to the office 2 - 3 days per week. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>What You’ll Do</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow Horizon3.ai’s META Commercial business by winning new customers, developing productive channel partnerships and helping organisations realise value from our cybersecurity solutions.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Win new accounts and expand our customer base by introducing disruptive cybersecurity software solutions to the META market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and convert a qualified pipeline, owning the sales cycle from qualification and proof of value through negotiation and close, with the goal of exceeding quota consistently quarter over quarter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn channel partnerships into revenue by proactively engaging regional resellers and developing joint opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrate Horizon3.ai solutions in virtual and in-person meetings, connecting technical capabilities to customer needs and business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive the post-proof of value ROI process, helping customers understand business value while building relationships that support satisfaction and retention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain accurate customer records, pipeline data and forecasts in Salesforce so opportunities, risks and next steps are clearly understood.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work independently to progress opportunities while collaborating with distributed sales, support and customer success teams to deliver a coordinated customer experience.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3>What You’ll Bring</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 3-5 years of successful cybersecurity sales experience, with a track record of driving growth, introducing disruptive software solutions and consistently exceeding quarterly quotas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previous experience selling technical solutions into the META region.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience establishing and monetising channel partnerships; existing relationships with key regional resellers are essential.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency across the full sales process, including qualification, proof of value, forecasting, negotiation, deal closure and post-proof of value ROI management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to present and demonstrate cybersecurity solutions effectively, both virtually and in person.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong CRM discipline and experience maintaining accurate pipeline records and forecasts in Salesforce (SFDC).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Challenger Question-Based Selling-type methodologies and sales tools such as <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://outreach.io/">Outreach</a>, LinkedIn Sales Navigator, ZoomInfo and Slack.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to work independently and collaborate effectively with distributed teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English and Arabic; additional language skills such as French are welcomed.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Travel Required</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a hybrid company, and this job will require you to spend 3 days based at our Amsterdam city centre sales hub. The role may require up to 40% of travel within the assigned territory to be successful. Job-related travel expenses are reviewed and must be approved by your manager.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks of </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Horizon3.ai"><strong>Horizon3.ai</strong></a></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Inclusive Team: We value diversity and promote an inclusive culture where everyone can thrive.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth Opportunities: Be part of a dynamic and growing team with numerous career development opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Innovative Culture: Work in a collaborative environment that encourages creativity and out-of-the-box thinking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote Work: We are a 100% remote company. Enjoy the flexibility to work in the way that supports you and brings out your best.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Compensation: We offer competitive salary, equity and benefits. Our benefits include health, vision &amp; dental insurance for you and your family, a flexible vacation policy, and generous parental leave.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You Belong Here</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Horizon3.ai">Horizon3.ai</a> is not just an equal opportunity employer - we are a community that values diversity, equity, and inclusion as fundamental principles of our culture and success. We are dedicated to fostering a workplace where everyone feels welcome and respected, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, hair length or any other legally protected status by law.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our commitment to diversity and inclusion means we strive to attract, develop, and retain a workforce that reflects the varied communities we serve. We believe that diverse perspectives drive innovation and strengthen our ability to create cutting-edge cybersecurity solutions. At <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Horizon3.ai">Horizon3.ai</a>, every team member is valued and supported in an environment that encourages personal and professional growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We welcome candidates from all backgrounds and experiences, and we encourage all qualified individuals to apply. Come be a part of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Horizon3.ai">Horizon3.ai</a>, where your unique contributions are recognized, and your potential is limitless.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Other Duties</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application Note</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In any materials you submit, you may redact or remove age-identifying information such as age, date of birth, or dates of school attendance or graduation. You will not be penalized for redacting or removing this information.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/horizon3ai/commercial-account-executive-meta-amsterdam-300572","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam, Netherlands","created_at":1795534817},{"slug":"executive-assistant-team-experience-lead-amsterdam-288724","company_name":"Prosus","title":"Executive Assistant & Team Experience Lead","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who We Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've ordered dinner through Just Eat Takeaway. You've bought and sold on OLX. You've paid with PayU. Chances are, you've already used a Prosus company today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are Prosus, a global technology company powering some of the world's leading lifestyle ecommerce businesses. Every day, billions of people across India, Latin America, Europe and beyond use our products and services to buy, sell, pay, connect and discover.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AI-driven ecosystem spans 100+ companies across ecommerce, food delivery, fintech and experiences, serving billions of consumers worldwide. AI powers how we operate and innovate, with more than 60,000 active AI agents helping our teams build, scale and move faster. Through our investment team, we also back the founders and technologies shaping the future: From robotics and autonomous systems to synthetic biology and frontier AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guided by our five values <strong>Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship,</strong> culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation; we build, we test, we learn, we iterate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of technology at global scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prosus is continuing to evolve its business, product and investment activities, with ambitious plans to build, scale and grow technology-driven businesses and products globally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a highly organised, proactive and resourceful Executive Assistant to provide high-quality executive and operational support to three senior leaders: the Chief Product Officer, the Head of Ventures, and the Director of Strategy &amp; Operations.  This is a varied and fast-paced role that sits close to the heart of the business. You will play an important part in enabling these leaders to operate effectively, ensuring their time and priorities are managed efficiently and that the day-to-day running of their respective areas is seamless.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will take ownership of complex calendars, international travel, meeting preparation, stakeholder coordination and administrative processes, while anticipating needs, managing competing priorities and identifying opportunities to improve how things are done. Working across different teams and functions, you will build strong relationships throughout the organisation and act as a trusted point of contact for both internal and external stakeholders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for someone who combines exceptional organisational skills with sound judgement, discretion and a hands-on approach. Someone who enjoys being one step ahead, takes pride in making things happen and thrives in an environment where priorities can move quickly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Will Do</strong></p><h3><strong>Executive &amp; Business Support</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide proactive, high-quality executive assistance to the Chief Product Officer, Head of Ventures, and Director of Strategy &amp; Operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage complex and frequently changing calendars, prioritising meetings, resolving scheduling conflicts and ensuring leaders make the best use of their time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate domestic and international travel arrangements, including flights, accommodation, ground transportation, detailed itineraries and visa requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage meeting logistics, including scheduling, preparing agendas, coordinating pre-reads and ensuring relevant materials are available ahead of time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Capture key actions and follow up with relevant stakeholders to ensure commitments and deliverables are progressing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted first point of contact for internal and external stakeholders, handling requests with professionalism, sound judgement and discretion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively anticipate the needs of the executives, identifying potential scheduling conflicts, upcoming priorities and opportunities to improve efficiency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage expenses, invoices, budget tracking and other administrative processes, ensuring accuracy and compliance with company policies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle confidential and sensitive information with the highest level of discretion and professionalism.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"> <strong>Stakeholder &amp; Operational Coordination</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong working relationships with colleagues and stakeholders across Product, Ventures, Strategy &amp; Operations and the wider Prosus organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate leadership meetings, workshops, offsites and other business events, managing logistics and ensuring smooth execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the coordination of cross-functional initiatives, helping ensure meetings, communications and follow-up actions are organised and delivered effectively.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist with onboarding and administrative arrangements for new team members and other relevant stakeholders across the supported functions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate with HR, Finance, IT, Workplace, Legal and other internal teams to resolve requests and ensure efficient day-to-day operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify opportunities to simplify administrative processes, improve ways of working and create greater efficiency for the executives and their teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide general operational support across the three functions, stepping in where needed to keep priorities moving and ensure nothing falls through the cracks.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a highly organised, proactive and solutions-oriented professional who enjoys working closely with senior leaders and making their lives easier.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You naturally think several steps ahead, have a strong sense of ownership and are comfortable managing multiple priorities in a fast-moving environment. You know when to take initiative, when to escalate and how to exercise sound judgement without needing constant direction.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are confident in engaging with senior stakeholders, build relationships easily and communicate clearly and professionally. You are equally comfortable managing the finer details of a complex travel itinerary as you are coordinating a senior leadership meeting or resolving an unexpected scheduling challenge.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Above all, you are dependable, discreet and take pride in delivering excellent support. You enjoy being behind the scenes, making things happen and creating the conditions for others to perform at their best.</p><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in an Executive Assistant, Senior Personal Assistant or Executive Business Partner role, ideally supporting multiple senior executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a fast-paced, international and complex business environment, preferably within technology, investment or a corporate organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple complex calendars and competing priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong experience coordinating international travel, meetings, leadership events and other executive-level logistics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the confidence to interact professionally with senior stakeholders and external partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive, hands-on mindset, with the ability to anticipate needs, solve problems independently and take ownership of tasks from start to finish.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong attention to detail and the ability to maintain accuracy while working at pace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High levels of discretion, integrity and professionalism when handling confidential and sensitive information.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working across different teams and functions, building relationships and navigating a complex organisational environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in Microsoft Office and other relevant productivity and collaboration tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English, both written and spoken.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Prosus?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Prosus, your colleagues include 60,000 AI agents… and your job is to figure out what that actually means. We're one of the largest operators of agentic AI on the planet, inside a $100B+ portfolio across 100+ companies and two billion people. The humans here own what AI can't do alone: judgment, creativity, and the call on what gets built next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Own the impact. Work the ecosystem. Earn your growth. Build with backing.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Curious about our perks and benefits? Take a look </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://prosusbenefits.com/"><em><u>at this page</u></em></a><em>.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Diversity &amp; Inclusion Commitment</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We respect the dignity and human rights of individuals and communities wherever we operate in the world. Building an inclusive workplace where everyone feels welcome and can thrive is critical for us. We provide access to education, which helps everyone understand the important role they play and the positive impact they can have.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Want to know more about life at Prosus? Explore our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.prosus.com/the-prosus-way"><em>culture and values</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/prosus/executive-assistant-team-experience-lead-amsterdam-288724","tags":["Product"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795534817},{"slug":"program-manager-office-of-the-chief-product-officer-amsterdam-354679","company_name":"Prosus","title":"Program Manager, Office of the Chief Product Officer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who We Are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've ordered dinner through Just Eat Takeaway. You've bought and sold on OLX. You've paid with PayU. Chances are, you've already used a Prosus company today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are Prosus, a global technology company powering some of the world's leading lifestyle ecommerce businesses. Every day, billions of people across India, Latin America, Europe and beyond use our products and services to buy, sell, pay, connect and discover.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AI-driven ecosystem spans 100+ companies across ecommerce, food delivery, fintech and experiences, serving billions of consumers worldwide. AI powers how we operate and innovate, with more than 60,000 active AI agents helping our teams build, scale and move faster. Through our investment team, we also back the founders and technologies shaping the future: From robotics and autonomous systems to synthetic biology and frontier AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guided by our five values <strong>Innovation, Results, People, Impact, and Entrepreneurship,</strong> culture is our competitive advantage. We thrive with experimentation; we build, we test, we learn, we iterate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join us in shaping the future of technology at global scale.</p><h2><strong>The Opportunity</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The CPO office at Prosus is deliberately small. Nalden sets the direction: what we build and why. Jons, as Chief of Staff, creates the traction: the operating model, the portfolio, the prioritisation, and the decisions that turn direction into shipped product. Around them sit product managers, product marketing, growth, brand, content and design, and three product pods that do the building.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What holds those two ends together is the work itself: every initiative visible, owned and moving, and every decision captured before it evaporates. That is this job. As Program Manager you run Nalden_OS — the operating loop of the CPO portfolio — day to day. You do not own the initiatives; you make sure each one has someone who does.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You join while that loop is being built rather than maintained, so you shape it: what gets tracked, how reviews run, what a decision record looks like, and which reporting we stop doing because nobody reads it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>In this role you will</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the whole portfolio visible, with an explicit owner on every line of work in flight across the CPO office and the product pods.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare the decisions: shape ambiguous work until it is ready to be decided on, and prepare the prioritisation calls and operating reviews for the CPO and the Chief of Staff.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make it move: track progress and dependencies across teams, surface blockers early, and escalate with a recommendation rather than a status update.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make it stick: capture decisions and the reasoning behind them, keep the information people rely on accurate, and turn what teams learn into knowledge someone will reuse.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the view: a clean, reliable portfolio in slides, backed by a tracking system people actually update — assembled with AI so it takes an hour, not a week.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the honest signal: say early where the plan and reality have diverged, including when the useful version is the uncomfortable one.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What This Role Is Not</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You do not make product decisions, approve teams' work, or become a reporting layer between teams and leadership. If teams spend more time updating you than shipping, the role is failing — and you would be the first to say so.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who You Are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are the person others trust in a messy week. When priorities shift and work stalls, you stay level, name what is actually happening, and get the loop closed. You follow up without nagging, and an unowned item bothers you until somebody picks it up.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You like order, but you fit the system to the work rather than the other way round. You build trust quickly across designers, engineers and executives, and you carry influence without authority: you move work through people who do not report to you. You are direct enough to raise the awkward problem early, and low-ego enough to let someone else take the credit when it lands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You Bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8 to 10 years running cross-team program execution in digital commerce, technology product management, consumer facing technology, with an earlier career in management consulting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have owned outcomes across teams without owning the teams. Titles vary — program manager, strategy manager, operations lead, product operations — but the pattern is the same: you were accountable for work you moved through people who did not report to you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in product work: you know how discovery, design and shipping actually run, and you can talk to designers and engineers without a translator.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with data and tools: you build a clean portfolio view and a tracking system people trust, and you use AI to do the assembly faster than most.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working closely with senior leaders, ideally from an executive office or chief-of-staff environment; experience inside a larger corporate group around a small, fast team is a real advantage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable at both altitudes: you can run a room of executives in the morning and fix the tracking sheet in the afternoon.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and spoken English. Dutch is a plus, not a requirement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not a classic PMO profile. We want someone who clears the path, not someone who produces process.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Global Impact: Play a crucial role in shaping the future of global commerce. Be part of a dynamic ecosystem of tech-led companies across markets, from emerging disruptors to established platforms, all working to create positive change at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth Opportunities: Expand your expertise through high-stakes challenges within our diverse portfolio. You will gain access to a network of businesses, leaders, and learning opportunities that span continents and industries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Innovative Culture: Join a forward-thinking team that values strategic insights and bold ideas. You will operate at the intersection of venture-building, innovation, and investment, where experimentation is encouraged and cross-company collaboration drives breakthroughs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creative Environment: Engage in work that encourages creativity and constant improvement. We challenge assumptions, explore new frontiers, and believe great ideas can come from anywhere in our ecosystem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborative Atmosphere: Benefit from autonomy and self-management in a supportive, outcome-driven workspace. You will work alongside sharp, motivated peers across our portfolio, all united by a shared ambition to move the needle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid Work: Experience the satisfaction of our flexible model tailored to balance work and life.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Compensation: Enjoy a salary package that reflects your skills and contributions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive Benefits: From health and wellness to learning, commuting, and everyday perks, we offer a well-rounded package designed to help you thrive at work and beyond.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Prosus?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Prosus, your colleagues include 60,000 AI agents… and your job is to figure out what that actually means. We're one of the largest operators of agentic AI on the planet, inside a $100B+ portfolio across 100+ companies and two billion people. The humans here own what AI can't do 