tegic partnership with one of the leading frontier AI labs, a Series A led by Andreessen Horowitz, and a $5B AI Infrastructure Fund, Volta is building the infrastructure layer of the AI era from the ground up. We are 100+ people across London, Palo Alto, and New York, with rapid growth expectations to hundreds.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About The Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commissioning is where an AI factory becomes real. As Senior Director, Global Commissioning &amp; Handover, you will lead commissioning of DSX facilities and network across all of Volta's sites, taking each one to ready for service and handing it over to our operations teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will build and lead a global team that owns Volta's commissioning standards for electrical, mechanical and CDU scopes, systems security, commissioning planning, facilities readiness and operational readiness. Your team sets how commissioning is done on every site, from tagging through to the turn-up sequence, and holds the schedule that takes each facility live.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time to market matters here. You will align commissioning to the turn-up sequence so that commissioning accelerates service rather than delays it, and you will make sure that when a building is handed over, the operations team, the procedures and the systems are ready to run it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Will Be Doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead commissioning of DSX facilities and network infrastructure across Volta's AI factories, taking each site to ready for service.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and lead the global Commissioning and Handover team, covering electrical, mechanical and CDU commissioning standards, systems security, commissioning planning, facilities readiness and operational readiness.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own Volta's commissioning standards for each discipline, from tagging and method statements through each commissioning level to the turn-up sequence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own CDU installation and commissioning standards, including handover to operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the commissioning schedule for every site and its alignment to turn-up, so that commissioning is never the critical path to service.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver the physical and systems security requirements for each site from construction through to handover.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the facilities readiness and operational readiness standards and governance, so each facility is ready for operations and the operations team is ready to run it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead handover into service, working with DC Operations on acceptance, documentation and training.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with Design and Engineering, the regional delivery teams and the DSX execution and network teams so commissioning is integrated into the master schedule on every site.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report commissioning progress and risk across sites, and feed lessons learned back into the standards and the reference design.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading commissioning of hyperscale data centres, including electrical, mechanical and liquid cooling systems. Data centre experience is essential.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record owning commissioning and handover across multiple concurrent sites at this level, and the ability to run it from day one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep knowledge of commissioning levels, integrated systems testing and the turn-up sequence for high density GPU environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with CDU and liquid cooling commissioning and handover into operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience setting readiness governance and handing live facilities over to operations teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and leading commissioning teams and managing commissioning agents and contractors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of physical and systems security requirements in mission critical facilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to travel to sites across Europe and North America.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">REQ-263</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Volta, we believe people do their best work when they feel supported, trusted and able to grow. We're building a company where you can make an impact, keep a healthy balance between work and life, and build a career you're proud of. <br />As a global team, we do our best to provide great benefits wherever you're based. While some benefits vary by country due to local regulations, we believe looking after our people is simply the right thing to do.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary based on the work you do here, not your previous salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity in Volta, giving you the opportunity to share in the company's long-term success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Retirement/pension contributions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive health, wellbeing and insurance benefits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous number of vacation days each year</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Additional Information</strong>